    "text": "1.0 Scope of this chapter The objective of general purpose financial reporting is the foundation of the Conceptual Framework; every other aspect flows from it. Other aspects of the Conceptual Framework—the qualitative characteristics of, and the cost constraint on, useful financial information, a reporting entity concept, elements of financial statements, recognition and derecognition, measurement, presentation and disclosure—flow logically from the objective. CF 2018 · para 1.1 EY iGAAP 2026 Ch2 · section 4 Chapter 1 carries over the 2010 text largely as it was, but now gives more prominence to the information users need to assess management’s stewardship. 2018 Change — stewardship reinstated in an otherwise largely unchanged chapter. Chapter 1 is largely unchanged from the 2010 Framework. The Board reintroduced the term stewardship and gave more prominence to the information users need to assess management’s stewardship (see 1.4 ). DTT A2 2022 · 4 CF 2018 · para BC1.32–BC1.33 Pitfall: quoting the objective sentence without its three decision types and its two assessments. CF 2018 · para 1.2–1.4"
