    "chapter": "Chapter 10 — Carve-out financial statements",
    "href": "../cf-2018/draft-v1-linked/ch10.html#s-10-0",
    "text": "10.0 Scope of this chapter Carve-out financial statements report on a portion of a larger entity — a division or lesser business component viewed as “carved out” of the larger consolidated financial statements. The Framework does not use the term; it allows a reporting entity to be a portion of an entity and sets the boundary tests that apply when the reporting entity is not a legal entity. CF 2018 · para 3.10 CF 2018 · para 3.13–3.14 PwC MOA 2020 · A2.5 PwC MOA 2020 · A2.17 KPMG Combined/Carve 2022 · 1.3 Official wording uses “portion of an entity” while “carve-out” is firm vocabulary, and a carve-out can also be combined. Portion of an entity is Official; carve-out is firm vocabulary. A reporting entity could be a portion of a legal entity, such as a branch or the activities within a defined region. See also 3.5 Reporting entity CF 2018 · para 3.10 DTT A2 2022 · 6.2 A carve-out can also be combined. Carve-out financial statements may also be combined financial statements — for example, when financial information from components of separate legal sub-groups is aggregated. See also Illus 9.5.2 PwC MOA 2020 · A2.5 KPMG Combined/Carve 2022 · Example 1D See also 3.5 Reporting entity 3.6 Reporting entity boundary Ch9 Combined FS Ch11 Status"
