    "chapter": "Chapter 2 — Recognition",
    "href": "../ias-16/draft-v1-linked/ch02.html#s-2-9",
    "text": "2.9 Recognition checklist / capitalise vs expense Question If yes → Cite Probable future economic benefits + cost reliably measurable? Recognition criteria met — continue IAS 16 · para 7 Spare / stand-by / servicing item meets PPE definition (incl. >1 period)? PPE; else inventory (IAS 2) IAS 16 · para 8 Individually insignificant items (moulds, tools, dies)? May aggregate; apply criteria to aggregate IAS 16 · para 9 Safety / environmental item enabling benefits from related assets? Capitalise; review combined CA under IAS 36 IAS 16 · para 11 Day-to-day servicing / repairs and maintenance / small parts? Expense in P&L IAS 16 · para 12 Cost of replacing a part, criteria met? Capitalise replacement; derecognise replaced CA IAS 16 · para 13 Major inspection / overhaul performed, criteria met? Capitalise as replacement; derecognise remaining prior inspection CA IAS 16 · para 14 Relocating / reorganising operations after asset capable of operating as intended? Not in PPE carrying amount IAS 16 · para 20 Disclaimer — personal study pack. These IAS 16 pages are personal study notes for private learning. They are not accounting, legal, or professional advice, and are not for commercial or mass redistribution. Official Standards remain authoritative. Big4 / firm-manual extracts and third-party financial-statement examples appear only as short teaching paraphrase or cited figures for private study; the pack owner has legal counsel. Do not treat this site as a substitute for the Official text, firm manuals, or issuer financial statements."
