    "href": "../ias-16/draft-v1-linked/ch03.html#s-3-3",
    "text": "3.3 Costs that are not included Examples of costs that are not costs of an item of PPE are: costs of opening a new facility; costs of introducing a new product or service (including advertising and promotional activities); costs of conducting business in a new location or with a new class of customer (including staff training); and administration and other general overhead costs. IAS 16 · para 19 PwC MOA 2020 Ch22 · 22.21 DTT iGAAP 2022 A7 · 4.2.1.2 EY iGAAP 2026 Ch19 · section 4.1.3 KPMG Insights 2019/20 · 3.2 · 3.2.50.10 Official exclusion list (para 19). (a) costs of opening a new facility; (b) costs of introducing a new product or service (including advertising and promotional activities); (c) costs of conducting business in a new location or with a new class of customer (including costs of staff training); and (d) administration and other general overhead costs. IAS 16 · para 19 Feasibility before commitment (PwC / KPMG). Costs of a feasibility study before deciding whether to invest, or which asset to acquire, are expensed — they are not linked to a specific PPE item. Once feasibility is established and the entity has committed, qualifying development-stage costs may be capitalised. Planning permission may fall in either stage depending on judgement. PwC MOA 2020 Ch22 · FAQ 22.21.1 KPMG Insights 2019/20 · 3.2 · 3.2.30.60 General business permits (KPMG). Opening a new plant in a new town: environmental certificate specific to the plant may be analysed carefully, but general permits that merely allow the entity to conduct business in the town are general business costs — not capitalised. KPMG Insights 2019/20 · 3.2 · Example 3A IAS 16 · para 19 Initial operating losses / under-capacity. Losses while demand builds up, or while an asset capable of operating as intended runs below full capacity, are not capitalised (see also para 20). IAS 16 · para 20(a)–(b) KPMG Insights 2019/20 · 3.2 · Example 3B PwC MOA 2020 Ch22 · FAQ 22.22.2 Overheads (PwC / DTT). Administration and other general overheads are not PPE cost. For self-constructed assets, only directly attributable costs — not a systematic allocation of fixed production overheads of the IAS 2 conversion type — enter PPE cost (see 3.6 ). PwC MOA 2020 Ch22 · FAQ 22.21.3 DTT iGAAP 2022 A7 · 4.2.2.1-1 IAS 16 · para 19(d)"
