    "href": "../ias-16/draft-v1-linked/ch03.html#s-3-10",
    "text": "3.10 IAS 23 borrowing-costs see-also tip Borrowing costs on qualifying assets. Borrowing costs that are directly attributable to the acquisition, construction or production of a qualifying asset are capitalised as part of the cost of that asset under IAS 23. A qualifying asset necessarily takes a substantial period of time to get ready for its intended use or sale. IAS 16 · para 22 points to IAS 23 for interest on self-constructed PPE. Unwinding of a decommissioning discount is not a borrowing cost under IAS 23. This chapter does not deep-dive IAS 23 (commencement, suspension, cessation, specific vs general borrowings). IAS 16 · para 22 IAS 23 · para 8 IAS 23 · para 5 PwC MOA 2020 Ch22 · 22.42–22.45 EY iGAAP 2026 Ch19 · section 4.1.2 KPMG Insights 2019/20 · 3.2 · 3.2.30.20 PwC MOA 2020 Ch22 · 22.31 See also — IAS 23 Borrowing Costs. Qualifying-asset borrowing costs can enter PPE cost — dashed tip beside elements of cost only. IAS 23"
