    "href": "../ias-16/draft-v1-linked/ch03.html#s-3-11",
    "text": "3.11 Initial-measurement checklist Question If yes → Cite Item qualifies for recognition as PPE? Measure at cost (Chapter 2 first) IAS 16 · para 15 Purchase price (duties, non-refundable taxes, net of discounts/rebates)? Include in cost IAS 16 · para 16(a) Cost directly attributable to location/condition for intended use? Include (employee benefits, site prep, delivery, install, testing, professional fees) IAS 16 · para 16(b) IAS 16 · para 17 Opening facility / new product / new location / admin overhead / training? Expense — not PPE cost IAS 16 · para 19 Asset already capable of operating as intended? Stop capitalising; expense further use / redeploy / under-capacity / initial losses / relocate IAS 16 · para 20 Items produced & sold while bringing asset to intended use? Proceeds + IAS 2 cost → P&L (do not net against PPE); disclose under 74A if required IAS 16 · para 20A IAS 16 · para 74A Incidental operations not necessary for intended use (e.g. site car park)? Income and expenses → P&L classifications IAS 16 · para 21 Self-constructed? Same principles; eliminate internal profits; exclude abnormal waste; IAS 23 if qualifying IAS 16 · para 22 Present dismantling / restoration obligation on acquisition or non-inventory use? Include initial estimate in cost (IAS 37 measure); inventory-use → IAS 2 IAS 16 · para 16(c) IAS 16 · para 18 Payment deferred beyond normal credit terms? Cost = cash-price equivalent; difference = interest (unless IAS 23) IAS 16 · para 23 Customer contributes PPE to facilitate contract fulfilment? IFRS 15 control test; if controlled, PPE at fair value, or at stand-alone selling price if fair value is not reasonably estimable — 3.1A IAS 16 · para 15 KPMG Insights 2019/20 · 3.2 · 3.2.20.40 IFRS 15 Purchase price includes amounts contingent on a future event? Test whether the payment relates to asset cost. Two observed approaches; no single Standard answer — 3.7A , differ table , Illustration 3.7A.2 PwC MOA 2020 Ch22 · 22.32 PwC MOA 2020 Ch22 · 22.33 EY iGAAP 2026 Ch19 · section 4.1.9 Customer reimburses part of a PPE transformation under a supply contract? IFRS 15 revenue (defer, then recognise); PPE at the full transformation cost, with no offset — Illustration 3.2.6 DTT iGAAP 2022 A7 · 4.2.6.1-1 IFRS 15 IAS 16 · para 16 Broker rebates seller-paid commission to the property purchaser? Component of property cost, not immediate income — Illustration 3.2.7 DTT iGAAP 2022 A7 · 4.2.7-1 IAS 16 · para 16 One-off capacity fee for extra utility quantities? Transferable between buildings → IAS 38 intangible. Attached and not transferable → building cost, depreciated — Illustration 3.2.8 DTT iGAAP 2022 A7 · 4.2.8-1 IAS 38 IAS 16 · para 16 Building physically complete, occupation approval still outstanding? Capitalise customary-period management costs and borrowing costs until approval; an avoidable delay is limited to the customary window — Illustration 3.2.9 DTT iGAAP 2022 A7 · 4.2.9-2 IAS 16 · para 16(b) IAS 23 · para 25 Environmental removal obligation arises only after acquisition? Paragraph 16 does not specifically address it (BC14). If paragraph 7 is met, capitalise the IAS 37 provision; the legislation is an impairment indicator — Illustration 3.4.2 DTT iGAAP 2022 A7 · 4.2.10-1 IAS 16 · para 7 IAS 37 Non-monetary exchange? FV unless no commercial substance or FV not reliably measurable; else CA given up IAS 16 · para 24–26 Government grant related to the asset? May reduce carrying amount under IAS 20 IAS 16 · para 28 Disclaimer — personal study pack. These IAS 16 pages are personal study notes for private learning. They are not accounting, legal, or professional advice, and are not for commercial or mass redistribution. Official Standards remain authoritative. Big4 / firm-manual extracts and third-party financial-statement examples appear only as short teaching paraphrase or cited figures for private study; the pack owner has legal counsel. Do not treat this site as a substitute for the Official text, firm manuals, or issuer financial statements."
