    "chapter": "Chapter 4 — Subsequent measurement — models",
    "href": "../ias-16/draft-v1-linked/ch04.html#s-4-10",
    "text": "4.10 Compensation for impairment or loss — thin tip Compensation is a separate event. Compensation from third parties for items of PPE that were impaired, lost or given up shall be included in profit or loss when the compensation becomes receivable. Impairments/losses, claims/payments of compensation, and subsequent purchase or construction of replacements are separate economic events and are accounted for separately (IAS 36 impairment; IAS 16 derecognition; compensation in P&L when receivable; replacement cost under IAS 16). Not the spine of this models chapter — thin cross-link toward Derecognition / impairment events. IAS 16 · para 65 IAS 16 · para 66 KPMG Insights 2019/20 · 3.2 · 3.2.370 EY iGAAP 2026 Ch19 · section 5 See also — Derecognition / IAS 36. Loss or disposal of the item, and recognition of compensation when receivable, are separate from choosing cost vs revaluation. IAS 16 · para 65–66 IAS 16 · para 67"
