    "chapter": "Chapter 4 — Subsequent measurement — models",
    "href": "../ias-16/draft-v1-linked/ch04.html#s-4-11",
    "text": "4.11 Models checklist Question If yes → Cite Chosen cost or revaluation for each class? Apply that policy to the entire class IAS 16 · para 29 Changing the class policy between cost and revaluation? Cost → revaluation: current-period revaluation, comparatives not restated. Revaluation → cost: retrospective reversal — Changing between cost and revaluation (IAS 8) IAS 8 · para 17 KPMG Insights 2019/20 · 3.2 · 3.2.360.10 KPMG Insights 2019/20 · 3.2 · 3.2.360.20 Class defined by similar nature and use? Use Official examples as starting point; geography alone usually not enough IAS 16 · para 37 Revaluing one item in a class? Revalue the entire class simultaneously (or rolling within a short period, kept up to date) IAS 16 · para 36 IAS 16 · para 38 Cost model? Carry at cost − accum dep − accum impairment IAS 16 · para 30 Revaluation model? FV reliably measurable; sufficient regularity so CA ≈ FV at period-end IAS 16 · para 31 IAS 16 · para 34 Adjusting books on revaluation? Eliminate accum dep or restate gross (observable / proportionate) — same net gain/loss IAS 16 · para 35 Carrying amount increased? OCI surplus, except reverse prior P&L decrease of same asset IAS 16 · para 39 Carrying amount decreased? P&L, except to extent of surplus on same asset → OCI IAS 16 · para 40 Transfer surplus to RE? On derecognition and/or as used (extra dep); never through P&L IAS 16 · para 41 Owner-occupied in unit-linked fund / IFRS 17 underlying? Optional IAS 40 FV election; separate class (29A–29B) IAS 16 · para 29A–29B Possible impairment? Apply IAS 36 (not this chapter) IAS 16 · para 63 Change in existing decommissioning liability? IFRIC 1 — cost model adjusts asset cost; revaluation model adjusts surplus/deficit IFRIC 1 · para 5–6 Third-party compensation for impaired/lost PPE? P&L when receivable; separate from impairment / replacement IAS 16 · para 65–66 Disclaimer — personal study pack. These IAS 16 pages are personal study notes for private learning. They are not accounting, legal, or professional advice, and are not for commercial or mass redistribution. Official Standards remain authoritative. Big4 / firm-manual extracts and third-party financial-statement examples appear only as short teaching paraphrase or cited figures for private study; the pack owner has legal counsel. Do not treat this site as a substitute for the Official text, firm manuals, or issuer financial statements."
