    "chapter": "Chapter 5 — Depreciation",
    "href": "../ias-16/draft-v1-linked/ch05.html#s-5-9",
    "text": "5.9 Right-of-use depreciation tip IFRS 16 right-of-use assets often borrow IAS 16 depreciation requirements. Depreciation of a right-of-use asset begins at lease commencement. Useful life of non-removable leasehold improvements is determined under IAS 16.56–57; if the improvements are not expected to be used beyond the lease term, useful life equals the lease term (IFRS IC November 2019). Full lease accounting lives in IFRS 16 — dashed tip only. IFRS 16 IAS 16 · para 56–57 EY iGAAP 2026 Ch19 · section 5.4.4 DTT iGAAP 2022 A7 · 7.6.7 See also — IFRS 16 Leases. Recognition and measurement of right-of-use assets; IAS 16 depreciation mechanics often applied by reference. IFRS 16"
