    "text": "5.11 Depreciation checklist Question If yes → Cite Significant parts with different useful life / method? Depreciate each significant part separately; group only if useful life and method the same IAS 16 · para 43–45 Remainder after significant parts? Depreciate remainder separately (approximation OK) IAS 16 · para 46 Major inspection / overhaul embedded? Isolate component at current overhaul cost; depreciate to next inspection IAS 16 · para 14 Depreciable amount set? Cost (or substituted amount) − residual value IAS 16 · para 50 IAS 16 · para 6 Residual / useful life / method reviewed this year-end? Prospective estimate change if expectations differ IAS 16 · para 51 IAS 16 · para 61 Residual at or above carrying amount? Depreciation charge = zero until residual falls below carrying amount IAS 16 · para 54 Asset available for use? Begin depreciation (even if not yet used) IAS 16 · para 55 Idle / mothballed / retired from active use? Continue depreciation (unless fully depreciated or usage method with zero output) IAS 16 · para 55 Held for sale (IFRS 5) or derecognised? Cease at the earlier of those dates IAS 16 · para 55 Land versus buildings? Account separately; land usually not depreciated; limited-life land / restoration portion may be IAS 16 · para 58–59 Method reflects consumption? Straight-line / diminishing / units of production as appropriate IAS 16 · para 60–62 Revenue-based method proposed? Not appropriate (para 62A) IAS 16 · para 62A Charge capitalised into another asset? Include in that asset’s carrying amount (IAS 2 / IAS 38 paths) IAS 16 · para 48–49 Disclaimer — personal study pack. These IAS 16 pages are personal study notes for private learning. They are not accounting, legal, or professional advice, and are not for commercial or mass redistribution. Official Standards remain authoritative. Big4 / firm-manual extracts and third-party financial-statement examples appear only as short teaching paraphrase or cited figures for private study; the pack owner has legal counsel. Do not treat this site as a substitute for the Official text, firm manuals, or issuer financial statements."
