    "chapter": "Chapter 6 — Derecognition",
    "href": "../ias-16/draft-v1-linked/ch06.html#s-6-8",
    "text": "6.8 Derecognition checklist Question If yes → Cite Disposed of, or no future benefits expected from use or disposal? Derecognise carrying amount IAS 16 · para 67 Physical part, or undivided interest, disposed of? Allocate carrying amount (systematic basis, or the ownership fraction); gain/loss = proceeds − allocated carrying amount; IAS 16 path only if control of that part is ceded — 6.0A , Illustration 6.0A.1 IAS 16 · para 9 IAS 16 · para 67 IAS 16 · para 71 EY iGAAP 2026 Ch19 · section 7.3 Disposal by sale / lease / donation? Disposal date = recipient obtains control (IFRS 15) IAS 16 · para 69 Gain or loss on derecognition? Net disposal proceeds − CA → P&L; gains not revenue (default) IAS 16 · para 68 IAS 16 · para 71 Consideration amount / later changes? IFRS 15 transaction price (para 47–72) and changes guidance IAS 16 · para 72 Routinely sell items previously held for rental? Transfer to inventories at CA; proceeds = IFRS 15 revenue; IFRS 5 N/A IAS 16 · para 68A Sale and leaseback? Apply IFRS 16 (may override para 68 gain-in-P&L) IAS 16 · para 68 IFRS 16 Replacement part capitalised? Derecognise replaced CA (estimate via replacement cost if needed). No disposal proceeds → para 68/71 loss — 6.5 tip ; full plate see 2.6.2 IAS 16 · para 13 IAS 16 · para 70 IAS 16 · para 68 IAS 16 · para 71 Third-party compensation for impaired / lost / given-up PPE? P&L when receivable; separate from impairment, derecognition, replacement cost IAS 16 · para 65–66 Classified held for sale (IFRS 5)? Exit IAS 16 measurement; cease depreciation; measure under IFRS 5 IFRS 5 IAS 16 · para 55 Revalued asset disposed of? Surplus may transfer to RE (not through P&L) IAS 16 · para 41 Disclaimer — personal study pack. These IAS 16 pages are personal study notes for private learning. They are not accounting, legal, or professional advice, and are not for commercial or mass redistribution. Official Standards remain authoritative. Big4 / firm-manual extracts and third-party financial-statement examples appear only as short teaching paraphrase or cited figures for private study; the pack owner has legal counsel. Do not treat this site as a substitute for the Official text, firm manuals, or issuer financial statements."
