    "chapter": "Chapter 7 — Disclosure",
    "href": "../ias-16/draft-v1-linked/ch07.html#s-7-7",
    "text": "7.7 Optional useful information Users of financial statements may also find the following information relevant. Therefore, entities are encouraged to disclose these amounts — they are not mandatory. IAS 16 · para 79 PwC MOA 2020 Ch22 · 22.115 DTT iGAAP 2022 A7 · 11.2.3 EY iGAAP 2026 Ch19 · section 8.3 79(a) — carrying amount of temporarily idle PPE. 79(b) — gross carrying amount of any fully depreciated PPE that is still in use. 79(c) — carrying amount of PPE retired from active use and not classified as held for sale under IFRS 5. 79(d) — when the cost model is used, the fair value of PPE when this is materially different from the carrying amount. IAS 16 · para 79 Illustration: 7.7.1 — Idle PPE and postponed construction — when significance pushes disclosure DTT iGAAP 2022 A7 · 11.2.3-1 IAS 16 · para 74(b) IAS 16 · para 79(a) IAS 1 · para 112(c) Facts IFRIC (now the IFRS Interpretations Committee) was asked how far disclosures are required for PPE that is temporarily idle and for assets under construction when further construction has been postponed. The item was not taken onto the IFRIC agenda. IAS 16 · para 74(b) requires disclosure of expenditures recognised in the carrying amount of PPE in the course of construction; para 79(a) encourages disclosure of temporarily idle PPE. Assessment IAS 1 · para 112(c) requires notes information that is not presented elsewhere but is relevant to an understanding of the financial statements. In combination, IAS 16 and IAS 1 create an expectation that when the amount of idle assets or postponed construction projects becomes significant , those amounts will be separately disclosed. Conclusions recorded in the May 2009 IFRIC Update (DTT 11.2.3-1). Conclusion Para 79 is “encouraged,” but significance + IAS 1 relevance can effectively require separate disclosure of idle / postponed-CIP amounts. Do not treat 79(a) as forever optional once the balance is material to users. 74(b) CIP disclosure remains mandatory regardless of the idle analysis. See also — Chapter 5 Depreciation · begin/cease; IFRS 5. Idle / mothballed assets continue to be depreciated until held for sale or derecognised; 79(c) covers retired-but-not-IFRS-5 items. IAS 16 · para 55 IAS 16 · para 79(c) Climate / dissimilar-risk disaggregation (EY tip). EY notes that where PPE items have sufficiently dissimilar risk characteristics (including climate-related), it may be necessary to disaggregate information in the PPE disclosures — IASB staff examples illustrate applying existing IFRS requirements to climate-related uncertainties. EY iGAAP 2026 Ch19 · section 8.3 Right-of-use presentation (EY tip). Lessees present right-of-use assets either separately or within the same line as corresponding owned assets, with disclosure of which line if combined — IFRS 16 home; not expanded here. EY iGAAP 2026 Ch19 · section 8.4 IFRS 16"
