    "text": "1.2 Scope exclusions IAS 2 applies to all inventories except financial instruments and biological assets related to agricultural activity and agricultural produce at the point of harvest. Scope exclusions cover inventories outside IAS 2, financial assets held for trading, and agricultural activity and harvest. IAS 2 · para 2 Inventories excluded from the scope of IAS 2. IAS 2 applies to all inventories Raw materials Consumable supplies Work in progress And finished goods except Financial instruments (IAS 32 and IFRS 9) And biological assets related to agricultural activity and agricultural produce at the point of harvest (IAS 41) Paragraph 2(a) is deleted (IFRS 15 amended paragraph 2). IAS 2 · para 2 IAS 2 · para 40E IAS 2 · para IN6 DTT A11 2022 · 2.2 PwC MOA 2020 · 25.3 EY IGAAP 2026 · Ch23 · section 2.3 Financial assets held for trading. Financial assets, such as investments held for trading for short-term profit making, are not inventory. KPMG Insights 2019/20 · 3.8.10 IAS 2 · para 2(b) Agricultural activity and harvest. Agricultural activity includes Raising livestock Forestry Annual or perennial cropping Orchards and plantations Floriculture And aquaculture Agricultural produce is the harvested product of an entity’s biological assets; harvest is the detachment of produce from a biological asset or the cessation of a biological asset’s life processes. PwC MOA 2020 · 25.5 Harvested agricultural produce enters IAS 2 after the point of harvest. IAS 41 measures it at fair value less costs to sell at the point of harvest, and that amount is its cost at that date for applying IAS 2. See also IAS 41 Chapter 3, 3.8 IAS 2 · para 20 IAS 41 · para 13 PwC MOA 2020 · 25.5"
