    "chapter": "Chapter 3 — Initial measurement",
    "href": "../ias-2/draft-v1-linked/ch03.html#s-3-ex-pwc-252",
    "text": "Types of cost included in the cost of inventories or expensed Examples of costs included in inventories as direct or indirect production costs, and of costs expensed as selling and administrative costs; borrowing costs on inventories manufactured in large quantities on a repetitive basis are an accounting policy choice. The table gives examples, not an exhaustive list: direct costs include production materials, production labour, employment costs of direct labour (for example, pension costs) and normal amounts of materials wastage; indirect costs include supervisor salaries and employment costs, other indirect labour, indirect materials, the costs of running the factory, depreciation of production equipment and related facilities and property, and amortisation of related acquired intangibles; expenses include product research, abnormal wastage, selling costs, storage costs ( Illustration 3.6.1 ) and general management costs. PwC MOA 2020 · FAQ 25.25.2 IAS 2 · para 16 IAS 23 · para 4(b) EY IGAAP 2026 · Ch23 · section 3.1.3 Description of costs Include in inventory Expense Direct Indirect Selling & admin Production materials ✓ Production labour ✓ Employment costs of direct labour (e.g. pension costs) ✓ Normal amounts of materials wastage ✓ Supervisor salaries and employment costs ✓ Other indirect labour ✓ Indirect materials ✓ Maintenance, heat, light, some taxes (excl. income taxes) and other indirect costs of running factory ✓ Depreciation of production equipment and related facilities and property ✓ Amortisation of related acquired intangibles ✓ Product research ✓ Abnormal amounts of wastage, labour and other costs ✓ Selling costs ✓ Storage costs (see Illustration 3.6.1 ) ✓ General management costs ✓ Borrowing costs on inventories manufactured in large quantities on a repetitive basis — policy choice ✓ ✓ Borrowing costs on other qualifying categories under IAS 23 ✓"
