    "chapter": "Chapter 3 — Initial measurement",
    "href": "../ias-2/draft-v1-linked/ch03.html#s-3-5",
    "text": "3.5 Other costs Other costs may include non-production overheads and design costs for specific customers, amortisation of related development costs, and the fair value of a derivative on settlement of a purchase contract, but not selling and advertising costs. Non-production overheads and the costs of designing products for specific customers. Other costs are included in the cost of inventories only to the extent that they are incurred in bringing the inventories to their present location and condition. For example, it may be appropriate to include non-production overheads or the costs of designing products for specific customers in the cost of inventories. The cost of designing products for specific customers is included to the extent that such costs are recoverable. Any other costs directly related to bringing inventories to the point of sale and getting them ready for sale are also allocated to inventories. IAS 2 · para 15 PwC MOA 2020 · 25.24 DTT A11 2022 · 3.2.4.1 KPMG Insights 2019/20 · 3.8.220.10 KPMG Insights 2019/20 · 3.8.220 Amortisation of development costs related to a specific product or process. The costs of designing products for specific customers include, for example, the amortisation of development costs related to a specific product or process. KPMG Insights 2019/20 · 3.8.220.10 IAS 38 · para 97 Fair value of a derivative on the settlement date of a purchase contract. The cost of inventory may include the fair value of a derivative on the settlement date of a purchase contract that does not meet the own-use scope exception in IFRS 9, if the entity’s policy is to recognise the cost of inventory on a gross basis ( Illustration 3.2.10 ). KPMG Insights 2019/20 · 3.8.220.15 Selling and advertising costs — not included. Selling and advertising costs cannot be included in the cost of inventory ( 3.6 ). KPMG Insights 2019/20 · 3.8.220.20 IAS 2 · para 16(d)"
