    "chapter": "Chapter 3 — Initial measurement",
    "href": "../ias-2/draft-v1-linked/ch03.html#s-3-8",
    "text": "3.8 Cost of agricultural produce harvested from biological assets Fair value less costs to sell at the point of harvest is the cost of the inventories at that date for applying IAS 2. Agricultural produce enters IAS 2 at fair value less costs to sell at the point of harvest; the section defines agricultural activity, produce and harvest; and after harvest the entity either carries the produce at cost or, under well-established industry practice, at NRV. IAS 2 · para 20 PwC MOA 2020 · 25.5 DTT A11 2022 · 3.2.6 KPMG Insights 2019/20 · 3.8.270.10 EY IGAAP 2026 · Ch23 · section 2.3 Fair value less costs to sell at the point of harvest — the cost for IAS 2. In accordance with IAS 41 Agriculture inventories comprising agricultural produce that an entity has harvested from its biological assets are measured on initial recognition at their fair value less costs to sell at the point of harvest. This is the cost of the inventories at that date for application of this Standard. The fair value less costs to sell of agricultural produce at the date of harvest is the deemed cost of the produce for the purpose of applying IAS 2. IAS 2 · para 20 IAS 41 · para 13 DTT A11 2022 · 3.2.6 KPMG Insights 2019/20 · 3.8.270.10 Agricultural activity, agricultural produce and harvest. Agricultural activity includes Raising livestock Forestry Annual or perennial cropping Orchards and plantations Floriculture Aquaculture IAS 41 is applied to agricultural produce — the harvested product of an entity’s biological assets — at the point of harvest; the harvest is the detachment of produce from a biological asset or the cessation of a biological asset’s life process. IAS 2 applies thereafter. PwC MOA 2020 · 25.5 IAS 41 · para 13 IAS 2 · para 20 After harvest — at cost or, under well-established industry practice, at NRV. The extent to which IAS 2 applies to inventories of harvested produce depends on the accounting policy adopted. Accounting policy after harvest Measurement Where there is a well-established industry practice of carrying such inventories at NRV The measurement provisions of IAS 2 do not apply and changes in that value are recognised in profit or loss in the period in which they arise ( Chapter 1 · 1.3 ) If the entity chooses to carry them at cost They are measured at the lower of that cost and NRV PwC MOA 2020 · 25.6 PwC MOA 2020 · 25.7 IAS 2 · para 4 IAS 2 · para 9 From biological asset to inventory Before harvest — IAS 41 Biological asset (for example, an orchard or livestock) Point of harvest Agricultural produce measured at fair value less costs to sell (IAS 41 para 13) — the cost for IAS 2 (para 20) After harvest — IAS 2 At cost — lower of cost and NRV ( Chapter 4 ) Industry practice — at NRV, changes in profit or loss (para 4) Which amount is the cost of agricultural produce at the point of harvest for applying IAS 2?"
