    "chapter": "Chapter 3 — Initial measurement",
    "href": "../ias-2/draft-v1-linked/ch03.html#key-terms",
    "text": "Key terms Cost of inventories — all costs of purchase, costs of conversion and other costs incurred in bringing the inventories to their present location and condition (para 10) Costs of purchase — purchase price, import duties and non-recoverable taxes, transport, handling and other directly attributable costs, less trade discounts, rebates and similar items (para 11) Costs of conversion — costs directly related to the units of production, such as direct labour, plus a systematic allocation of fixed and variable production overheads (para 12) Fixed production overheads — indirect costs of production that remain relatively constant regardless of the volume of production (para 12) Variable production overheads — indirect costs of production that vary directly, or nearly directly, with the volume of production (para 12) Normal capacity — the production expected to be achieved on average over a number of periods or seasons under normal circumstances, taking into account planned maintenance (para 13) Joint products and by-products — more than one product from one production process; conversion costs allocated on a rational and consistent basis (para 14) Financing element — in deferred settlement terms, for example the difference between the purchase price for normal credit terms and the amount paid; recognised as interest expense (para 18) Standard cost method and retail method — techniques for measuring cost, used for convenience if the results approximate cost (paras 21–22) Specific identification — specific costs attributed to identified items; required for items not ordinarily interchangeable and items segregated for specific projects (paras 23–24) FIFO and weighted average — the cost formulas for other inventories; same formula for inventories of similar nature and use (paras 25–27) LIFO — not permitted (para IN13) References. IAS 2 Inventories. PwC MOA 2020 Ch25; DTT iGAAP 2022 A11; EY iGAAP 2026 Ch23; KPMG Insights 2019/20 · Part 1 · 3.8. Disclaimer — personal study pack. These IAS 2 pages are personal study notes for private learning. They are not accounting, legal, or professional advice, and are not for commercial or mass redistribution. Official Standards remain authoritative. Big4 / firm-manual extracts and third-party financial-statement examples appear only as short teaching paraphrase or cited figures for private study; the pack owner has legal counsel. Do not treat this site as a substitute for the Official text, firm manuals, or issuer financial statements."
