    "chapter": "Chapter 4 — Subsequent measurement",
    "href": "../ias-2/draft-v1-linked/ch04.html#key-terms",
    "text": "Key terms Lower of cost and net realisable value — the measurement of inventories after initial recognition at cost (para 9) Net realisable value — the estimated selling price in the ordinary course of business less the estimated costs of completion and the estimated costs necessary to make the sale; an entity-specific value (paras 6–7) Fair value — the price that would be received to sell an asset in an orderly transaction between market participants at the measurement date; not an entity-specific value (paras 6–7) Costs necessary to make the sale — not limited to incremental costs (June 2021 IFRIC Update) Item by item — the usual basis for writing inventories down; similar or related items may be grouped in some circumstances (para 29) Firm sales contracts — NRV of the quantity held to satisfy them is based on the contract price; the excess on general selling prices (para 31) Replacement cost — may be the best available measure of the NRV of materials (para 32) Reversal of a write-down — limited to the amount of the original write-down, so that the new carrying amount is the lower of cost and revised NRV (para 33) References. IAS 2 Inventories. PwC MOA 2020 Ch25; DTT iGAAP 2022 A11; EY iGAAP 2026 Ch23; KPMG Insights 2019/20 · Part 1 · 3.8. Disclaimer — personal study pack. These IAS 2 pages are personal study notes for private learning. They are not accounting, legal, or professional advice, and are not for commercial or mass redistribution. Official Standards remain authoritative. Big4 / firm-manual extracts and third-party financial-statement examples appear only as short teaching paraphrase or cited figures for private study; the pack owner has legal counsel. Do not treat this site as a substitute for the Official text, firm manuals, or issuer financial statements."
