    "chapter": "Chapter 6 — Disclosure",
    "href": "../ias-2/draft-v1-linked/ch06.html#s-6-0",
    "text": "6.0 Disclosure requirements The financial statements disclose the accounting policies adopted in measuring inventories, the carrying amounts of inventories and the amounts recognised in profit or loss listed in paragraph 36; paragraphs 37 to 39 deal with the classifications of inventories and with how the amount recognised as an expense is presented. Disclosure opens with the paragraph 36 list, notes that presentation and disclosure still apply where measurement is carved out, and flags cryptocurrencies held for sale in the ordinary course of business. IAS 2 · para 36 IAS 2 · para 37 IAS 2 · para 38 IAS 2 · para 39 PwC MOA 2020 · 25.47 DTT A11 2022 · 4.2 KPMG Insights 2019/20 · 3.8.400 Paragraph 36. The disclosure requirements for inventories are set out in paragraph 36 of IAS 2: Accounting policies, including the cost formula used The total carrying amount and its classifications The carrying amount carried at fair value less costs to sell The amount recognised as an expense Write-downs Reversals of write-downs and the circumstances or events that led to them The carrying amount pledged as security for liabilities IAS 2 · para 36 PwC MOA 2020 · 25.47 DTT A11 2022 · 4.2 Presentation and disclosure still apply. Inventories excluded from the measurement requirements. The presentation and disclosure requirements of IAS 2 apply to items of inventory held by producers of agricultural and forest products, agricultural produce after harvest and minerals and mineral products measured at net realisable value (NRV), and by commodity broker-traders, even though the measurement requirements do not ( Chapter 1 · 1.3 ). KPMG Insights 2019/20 · 3.8.70.40 KPMG Insights 2019/20 · 3.8.80.30 IAS 2 · para 3 IAS 2 · para 4 IAS 2 · para 5 Cryptocurrencies. An entity provides the disclosures required by paragraphs 36 to 39 for cryptocurrencies held for sale in the ordinary course of business; if it measures its holdings at fair value, it also provides the disclosures in IFRS 13 · para 91–99 , and it discloses significant judgements ( IAS 1 · para 122 ) and material non-adjusting events ( IAS 10 · para 21 ) ( Illustration 1.1.2 ). DTT A11 2022 · 2.1-3 IAS 2 · para 36–39 Disclosures and related paragraphs, by section. IAS 2 · para 36 IAS 2 · para 37 IAS 2 · para 38 IAS 2 · para 39 DTT A11 2022 · 4.2.1 DTT A11 2022 · 4.2.2 DTT A11 2022 · 4.2.4 DTT A11 2022 · 4.2.5 DTT A11 2022 · 4.2.6 The accounting policies adopted in measuring inventories, including the cost formula used ( 6.1 ). IAS 2 · para 36(a) The total carrying amount of inventories and the carrying amount in classifications appropriate to the entity ( 6.2 ). IAS 2 · para 36(b) IAS 2 · para 37 The carrying amount of inventories carried at fair value less costs to sell ( 6.3 ). IAS 2 · para 36(c) The amount of inventories recognised as an expense during the period ( 6.4 ). IAS 2 · para 36(d) IAS 2 · para 38 The amount of any write-down of inventories recognised as an expense in the period in accordance with paragraph 34 ( 6.4 ). IAS 2 · para 36(e) The amount of any reversal of any write-down that is recognised as a reduction in the amount of inventories recognised as expense in the period in accordance with paragraph 34 ( 6.4 ). IAS 2 · para 36(f) The circumstances or events that led to the reversal of a write-down of inventories in accordance with paragraph 34 ( 6.4 ). IAS 2 · para 36(g) The carrying amount of inventories pledged as security for liabilities ( 6.6 ). IAS 2 · para 36(h) Entities that analyse expenses by nature: costs recognised as an expense for raw materials and consumables, labour costs and other costs, together with the amount of the net change in inventories for the period ( 6.5 ). IAS 2 · para 39"
