    "text": "6.3 Inventories carried at fair value less costs to sell The financial statements disclose the carrying amount of inventories carried at fair value less costs to sell. Fair value less costs to sell disclosure applies to commodity broker-traders, inventories that remain measured under IAS 2 inside a disposal group, and cryptocurrencies measured at fair value. IAS 2 · para 36(c) IAS 2 · para IN16 DTT A11 2022 · 4.2.4 Commodity broker-traders. the carrying amount of inventories carried at fair value less costs to sell . The Standard requires disclosure of the carrying amount of inventories carried at fair value less costs to sell; in practice this requirement applies only to certain inventories held by commodity broker-traders ( Chapter 1 · 1.3 ). IAS 2 · para 36(c) IAS 2 · para IN16 DTT A11 2022 · 4.2.4 EY IGAAP 2026 · Ch23 · section 6.1 Still measured under IAS 2. When inventories are classified as held for sale as part of a disposal group, they continue to be measured in accordance with IAS 2; the disposal group itself may then be written down to fair value less costs to sell, but not the inventories per se. DTT A11 2022 · 4.2.4 Cryptocurrencies. If an entity measures holdings of cryptocurrencies at fair value, the disclosures specified in IFRS 13 · para 91–99 are provided ( Illustration 1.1.2 ). DTT A11 2022 · 2.1-3"
