    "chapter": "Chapter 1 — What’s new vs IAS 1",
    "href": "../ifrs-18/draft-v1-linked/ch01.html#s-1-0",
    "text": "1.0 Scope of this chapter Chapter 1 sets out what IFRS 18 changes relative to IAS 1 — why the IASB issued it, the three new requirement sets , what IAS 1 material was carried forward or moved, the new terminology, and the effective date. Quotations are taken from HKFRS 18, whose text is the same as IFRS 18; the pack labels everything IFRS 18. Detailed requirements on the primary financial statements and aggregation (Ch2), categories (Ch3), totals and subtotals (Ch4), operating expenses (Ch5), MPMs (Ch6), other statements (Ch7) and transition (Ch8) are taught in later chapters. IFRS 18 is the presentation and disclosure spine for general purpose financial statements. Its objective is relevant information that faithfully represents assets, liabilities, equity, income and expenses, matching IAS 1 for every IFRS preparer, while other Standards still set recognition and measurement. Presentation and disclosure only — recognition and measurement stay in other Standards: Objective This Standard sets out requirements for the presentation and disclosure of information in general purpose financial statements (financial statements) to help ensure they provide relevant information that faithfully represents an entity’s assets, liabilities, equity, income and expenses. The Introduction restates the same objective for the Standard as a whole. IFRS 18 · para 1 IFRS 18 · para IN1 Same objective as IAS 1; applies to every entity preparing IFRS financial statements: An entity shall apply this Standard in presenting and disclosing information in financial statements prepared in accordance with HKFRS Accounting Standards. The objective is the same as for its predecessor, and the requirements apply to consolidated and separate financial statements. IFRS 18 · para 2 EY Closer look 2026 · section 1.1 EY iGAAP 2026 Ch04 · section 1.1 Other Standards set recognition and measurement: Other HKFRS Accounting Standards set out the recognition, measurement, presentation and disclosure requirements for specific transactions and other events. IFRS 18 is the presentation and disclosure spine; recognition and measurement are not rebuilt here. IFRS 18 · para 4 EY Closer look 2026 · section 1.1 EY iGAAP 2026 Ch04 · section 1.1 Scope point Requirement Effect Pack home Statements covered General and specific requirements for the statement(s) of financial performance, the statement of financial position and the statement of changes in equity, plus requirements for disclosure in the notes. IFRS 18 · para 3 IFRS 18 also sets requirements for the descriptions (labels) of line items and items disclosed in the notes, categories and mandatory subtotals in the statement of profit or loss, and MPM disclosures in a single note. EY Closer look 2026 · section 1.1 EY iGAAP 2026 Ch04 · section 1.1 Ch2–Ch6 Statement of cash flows HKAS 7 Statement of Cash Flows sets out requirements for the presentation and disclosure of cash flow information. However, the general requirements for financial statements in paragraphs 9–43 and 113–114 apply to the statement of cash flows. IFRS 18 · para 3 IFRS 18 is now explicit that the general requirements, the aggregation and disaggregation principles and some note requirements apply to the statement of cash flows; IAS 7 itself receives narrow-scope amendments (see 1.3.3 ). EY Closer look 2026 · section 1.1 EY iGAAP 2026 Ch04 · section 1.1 Ch7 7.1 Condensed interim financial statements (IAS 34) IFRS 18 does not apply to condensed interim financial statements prepared applying IAS 34, However, paragraphs 41–45 and 117–125 apply to such financial statements. IFRS 18 · para 5 The aggregation and disaggregation principles and the MPM requirements reach condensed interim reports; first-year interim rules are in transition (see 1.4 ). EY Closer look 2026 · section 1.1 EY iGAAP 2026 Ch04 · section 1.1 Ch7 7.4 · Ch8 8.4 Not-for-profit and public sector entities Terminology suits profit-oriented entities, including public sector business entities; entities with not-for-profit activities may need to amend descriptions of line items, categories, subtotals or totals and of the financial statements themselves. IFRS 18 · para 6 The paragraph addresses descriptions (labels) only. — Entities without equity (IAS 32) Entities without equity as defined in IAS 32 (for example, some mutual funds) and entities whose share capital is not equity (for example, some co-operative entities) may need to adapt the presentation of members’ or unitholders’ interests. IFRS 18 · para 7 Presentation of members’ or unitholders’ interests adapts. — Financial review by management A financial review by management, separate from the financial statements, that describes the main features of financial performance and position and the principal uncertainties is outside the scope of HKFRS Accounting Standards. IFRS 18 · para 8 Management commentary is not part of the financial statements, but it is a public communication outside the financial statements — the setting in which MPMs are identified (Ch6). IFRS 18 · para IN14 Ch6 6.2 IFRS 18 supersedes IAS 1, with unchanged requirements moving to IFRS 18, IAS 8 and IFRS 7, and the IAS 1 baseline before IFRS 18 still frames what changed. IFRS 18 supersedes IAS 1; unchanged requirements move to IFRS 18, IAS 8 and IFRS 7: Transfer of unchanged IAS 1 requirements: HKFRS 18 supersedes HKAS 1 Presentation of Financial Statements. Requirements in HKAS 1 that are unchanged have been transferred to HKFRS 18, HKAS 8 Basis of Preparation of Financial Statements … and HKFRS 7 Financial Instruments: Disclosures. Site labels: IFRS 18 / IAS 1 / IAS 8 / IFRS 7. IFRS 18 · para IN3 Some IAS 1 general requirements continue under new homes: IFRS 18 replaces IAS 1; some IAS 1 requirements move to IAS 8 (renamed Basis of Preparation of Financial Statements ); other general requirements continue (for example, current/non-current classification and going-concern considerations). The KPMG Appendix maps each carried or moved topic without substantive change (reproduced as the paragraph bridge in 1.3.2 ). KPMG FI 2024 · section 1.1 fn1 · Appendix EY Closer look 2026 · Overview IAS 1 baseline before IFRS 18: What IAS 1 covered: overall requirements for financial statements — structure, general requirements for content, and overriding concepts such as going concern, the accrual basis of accounting and the current/non-current distinction; a complete set comprised a statement of financial position, a statement of profit or loss and other comprehensive income, a statement of changes in equity, a statement of cash flows and notes. The 2019 Exposure Draft (ED/2019/7) proposed replacing IAS 1 (see 1.1.1 ). Read it to recognise what IAS 1 taught; the IFRS 18 gaps it left are in 1.1. DTT A4 2022 · 1.1 IFRS 18 · para IN4–IN6 Pitfall: Rebuilding an IAS 1 pack under a new cover. Deloitte A4 is IAS 1 / pre-IFRS 18 bridge only — do not structure teaching as IAS 1. DTT A4 2022 · 1.1 IFRS 18 · para IN4–IN6"
