    "text": "1.3.1 — IFRS 18 on one page — what changed, what did not Figure 1 summarises IFRS 18 by area, separating requirements introduced by IFRS 18 from those carried forward from IAS 1 to IFRS 18 and other Standards. Figure 1 accompanies IFRS 18 and is not part of it; the paragraph ranges below are those printed in the figure. IFRS 18 · Figure 1 Area Status and content Pack home Objective of financial statements Provide information about assets, liabilities, equity, income and expenses useful for assessing the prospects for future net cash inflows and management’s stewardship of the entity’s economic resources. Ch2 IFRS 18 · para 9 Primary financial statements — role Provide useful structured summaries of assets, liabilities, equity, income, expenses and cash flows. Ch2 2.1 IFRS 18 · para 16, 18–24, B8–B9 Statement of profit or loss Changes introduced — IFRS 18 changes focus here (categories, subtotals, operating expense analysis). Ch3 – Ch5 IFRS 18 · para 46–50, 52–82, B29–B85 Statement of cash flows Limited changes to specific requirements (through IAS 7). Ch7 7.1 IFRS 18 · para 3 + IAS 7 Statement of financial position Limited changes to specific requirements — for example, goodwill becomes a separate line item because, as an unidentifiable asset measured only as a residual, it is sufficiently dissimilar from intangible assets. IFRS 18 · para 103(d) IFRS 18 · para BC314 KPMG FI 2024 · section 1.1 Ch7 7.2 IFRS 18 · para 96–106, B90–B111 Statement presenting comprehensive income No changes to specific requirements. 1.3.2 bridge IFRS 18 · para 86–95, B86–B89 Statement of changes in equity No changes to specific requirements. 1.3.2 bridge IFRS 18 · para 107–112 Cross-referencing Items in the primary financial statements are cross-referenced to related information in the notes; amounts in the notes are linked to the primary financial statements by disclosing the line item(s) that contain them. Ch2 IFRS 18 · para 114 General requirements Complete set of financial statements; identification of financial statements; frequency of reporting; consistency of presentation, disclosure and classification; comparative information; materiality. 1.3.2 · 1.3.4 · Ch2 IFRS 18 · para 10–14, 25–40, B1–B5, B10–B15 Aggregation and disaggregation Aggregate on shared characteristics and disaggregate on characteristics that are not shared; guidance on informative labels and on disclosing information about aggregated items. Ch2 2.3–2.4 IFRS 18 · para 41–45, B16–B28 Notes Presented systematically to provide material information needed to understand the line items in the primary financial statements and to supplement them; material information not presented in the primary financial statements is disclosed in the notes. Ch2 2.1 IFRS 18 · para 17–20, 113–116, B6–B7, B112 Disclosures introduced or amended Management-defined performance measures Specified expenses by nature Description of nature expenses included in each function line item Information on specified main business activities (investing in assets or providing financing to customers) Ch6 · Ch5 · Ch3 IFRS 18 · para 117–125, B113–B142 IFRS 18 · para 83–85, B84 IFRS 18 · para 82(b) IFRS 18 · para 51 Disclosures carried forward (examples) Basis of preparation — IAS 8 paras 6A–6N Material accounting policy information — IAS 8 paras 27A–27I Sources of estimation uncertainty — IAS 8 paras 31A–31I Capital management, share capital and dividends Liabilities with a right to defer settlement subject to covenants within 12 months after the reporting period Ch7 7.5 (capital) IFRS 18 · Figure 1 IFRS 18 · para 126–132 IFRS 18 · para B106"
