    "text": "1.3.3 — Consequential amendments to other Standards IFRS 18 makes narrow-scope but widely applicable amendments to other Standards, which must be adopted at the same time as IFRS 18. The amended text sits in those Standards rather than in IFRS 18. EY Closer look 2026 · Overview IFRS 18 · App D Standard Amendment Pack home IAS 7 Statement of Cash Flows Operating profit or loss becomes the mandatory starting point for the indirect method; the options for classifying interest and dividend cash flows are largely removed. IFRS 18’s general requirements (paras 9–43, 113–114) also apply to the statement of cash flows. KPMG FI 2024 · section 1.1 EY Closer look 2026 · Overview IFRS 18 · para 3 Ch7 7.1 IAS 8 Basis of Preparation of Financial Statements Retitled (formerly Accounting Policies, Changes in Accounting Estimates and Errors ); receives IAS 1 requirements on fair presentation and compliance, going concern, accrual basis, accounting policy disclosures and estimation uncertainty ( 1.3.2 ). IFRS 18 · para IN3 EY Closer look 2026 · Overview fn2 1.3.2 IFRS 7 Financial Instruments: Disclosures Receives, to a much lesser extent, IAS 1 requirements — disclosures on puttable financial instruments classified as equity. IFRS 18 · para IN3 EY Closer look 2026 · section 1 EY iGAAP 2026 Ch04 · section 1 1.3.2 IAS 33 Earnings per Share Restricts the types of additional earnings per share measures entities may disclose. EY Closer look 2026 · Overview Ch7 7.3 IAS 34 Interim Financial Reporting Requires the same MPM-related disclosures in interim financial statements as in annual financial statements. EY Closer look 2026 · Overview Ch7 7.4 IFRS 1, IAS 8 and IAS 34 — compliance references Amended to refer to the paragraphs on the statement of compliance with IFRS Accounting Standards; other references to IFRS, IFRSs or IFRS Standards elsewhere were left unchanged. IFRS 18 · para BC425 1.3.4"
