    "text": "1.3.4 — Terminology, statement titles and identification of the financial statements Some IFRS 18 terms differ from IAS 1, and IFRS 18 separates “present” from “disclose” ; identification requirements carry forward with updated guidance for electronic reporting. EY Closer look 2026 · section 1.2 EY Closer look 2026 · section 1.3 EY iGAAP 2026 Ch04 · section 1.3 Term or requirement IFRS 18 Change from IAS 1 Statement of financial performance The statement (or statements) of financial performance for the reporting period, presented either as a single statement of profit or loss and other comprehensive income (profit or loss section first, followed directly by the other comprehensive income section) or as a statement of profit or loss immediately followed by a separate statement presenting comprehensive income that begins with profit or loss. IFRS 18 · para 10(a) IFRS 18 · para 12 New umbrella term; IAS 1 referred to a “statement of profit or loss and other comprehensive income”. EY Closer look 2026 · section 1.2 “Statement of profit or loss” and “statement presenting comprehensive income” Each term covers both the section of a single statement and the separate statement. IFRS 18 · para 13 New defined usage. EY Closer look 2026 · section 1.2 EY iGAAP 2026 Ch04 · section 1.2 Primary financial statements and the complete set Statement(s) of financial performance, statement of financial position, statement of changes in equity and statement of cash flows (with comparatives) are the primary financial statements. A complete set adds notes, comparative information (paras 31–32) and an opening statement of financial position when para 37 requires it. IFRS 18 · para 10–11 New concept of “primary financial statements”. EY Closer look 2026 · section 1.2 EY iGAAP 2026 Ch04 · section 1.2 Titles and labels Other statement titles are allowed (for example, “balance sheet”); other labels for totals, subtotals and line items are allowed if they faithfully represent the items’ characteristics (para 43) — for example, “net income” for profit or loss. IFRS 18 · para 11 Any label used must faithfully represent the characteristics of the item (para 43). IFRS 18 · para 11 Equal prominence Each primary financial statement is presented with equal prominence in a complete set. IFRS 18 · para 14 Part of the general requirements for a complete set (paras 10–14). IFRS 18 · Figure 1 Present versus disclose …an entity presents information in the primary financial statements and discloses information in the notes. Only material information need be presented or disclosed. IFRS 18 · para 15 IAS 1 mostly used the two terms interchangeably; the title of IFRS 18 reflects the distinction. EY Closer look 2026 · section 1.2 EY iGAAP 2026 Ch04 · section 1.2 IFRS Accounting Standards Defined term: Standards issued by the IASB, comprising IFRSs, IASs, IFRIC Interpretations and SIC Interpretations; previously known as International Financial Reporting Standards, IFRS, IFRSs and IFRS Standards. IFRS 18 · App A IFRS 18 · para BC424 Replaces the IAS 1 definition of “International Financial Reporting Standards”, distinguishing the IASB’s Standards from IFRS Sustainability Disclosure Standards issued by the ISSB. EY Closer look 2026 · section 1.2 EY iGAAP 2026 Ch04 · section 1.2 Statement of compliance IAS 8 requires an explicit and unreserved statement of compliance with “IFRS Accounting Standards” in the notes. Under the IFRS Foundation Trade Mark Guidelines the set must be called “IFRS Accounting Standards”, not “IFRS” or “IFRSs”; local regulators may require otherwise, and the financial statements and the auditor’s opinion must use the same framework reference. EY Closer look 2026 · section 1.2 EY iGAAP 2026 Ch04 · section 1.2 Before IFRS 18 is effective, entities ought to consider using “IFRS Accounting Standards” in the IAS 1 compliance statement to distinguish it from IFRS Sustainability Disclosure Standards. EY Closer look 2026 · section 1.2 EY iGAAP 2026 Ch04 · section 1.2 Identification of the financial statements An entity shall clearly identify the financial statements and distinguish them from other information in the same published document ; IFRS Accounting Standards apply only to the financial statements, not necessarily to other information in an annual report or regulatory filing. IFRS 18 · para 25–26 Identify each primary financial statement and the notes; disclose prominently, and repeat when needed — the entity’s name or other identification (and changes since the preceding period end), individual entity or group, period end or period covered, presentation currency (IAS 21), and level of rounding: The entity’s name or other identification (and changes since the preceding period end) Individual entity or group Period end or period covered Presentation currency (IAS 21) Level of rounding IFRS 18 · para 27 Same requirement as IAS 1; application guidance updated so that an entity providing financial statements electronically considers other ways to meet the requirements — for example, by appropriate digital tagging . IFRS 18 · para B10 EY Closer look 2026 · section 1.3 EY iGAAP 2026 Ch04 · section 1.3"
