    "text": "1.3.5 — Net profit unchanged — the statement of profit or loss changes shape Net profit keeps the same bottom line under a new structure, and comparability builds over time because there is no live benchmark. The change comes through presentation rather than recognition or measurement, and a familiar net profit does not mean the teaching of the statement of profit or loss is unchanged. Same bottom line, new structure: Although companies’ net profit will remain unchanged, many will see changes to the structure of their income statement. For some, the changes will be significant, depending on their current presentation practice… KPMG FI 2024 · Foreword No live benchmark — comparability builds over time: IFRS 18 will affect all companies across different industries; with no live benchmark yet, comparability will build over time. KPMG FI 2024 · Foreword Achieved through presentation, not recognition or measurement: …more transparent and comparable information about entities’ financial performance… comes from categories, defined subtotals, grouping discipline and the MPM note, not from changing recognition or measurement. IFRS 18 · para IN6–IN7 IFRS 18 · para 4 IFRS 18 · para 69–72 Familiar net profit ≠ unchanged teaching of the statement of profit or loss: study the shape — category bands, defined subtotals and the MPM bridge — not only the total. IFRS 18 · para IN7–IN8 IFRS 18 · para IN15"
