    "text": "1.4 Effective date and transition IFRS 18 applies to annual periods beginning on or after 1 January 2027, with earlier application permitted and disclosed, and is applied retrospectively with first-year reconciliations. Annual periods beginning on or after 1 January 2027; earlier application permitted and disclosed: Effective date: An entity shall apply this Standard for annual reporting periods beginning on or after 1 January 2027. Earlier application is permitted. If an entity applies this Standard for an earlier period, it shall disclose that fact in the notes. IFRS 18 · para C1 IFRS 18 · para IN2 KPMG FI 2024 · section 7.1 Why 1 January 2027: the IASB weighed implementation time (including for jurisdictions to incorporate the requirements into law) against users’ need for the information as soon as possible; some entities said they need at least two years, and endorsement, translation and regulatory changes also take time. IFRS 18 · para BC414 IFRS 18 · para BC416 Consequential amendments at the same time: IFRS 18 and the consequential amendments to other Standards must be adopted together. EY Closer look 2026 · Overview Retrospective application with first-year reconciliations: Retrospective under IAS 8, with relief: apply retrospectively applying IAS 8; the quantitative information in IAS 8 para 28(f) is not required. Retrospective restatement avoids misleading comparatives given extensive changes to the statement of profit or loss; because only presentation and disclosure change, periods before the earliest comparative period need not be considered. IFRS 18 · para C2 IFRS 18 · para BC417 Annual reconciliation: for the comparative period immediately preceding first application, reconcile each line item in the statement of profit or loss between the restated IFRS 18 amounts and the amounts previously presented under IAS 1. IFRS 18 · para C3 First-year interim: condensed interim financial statements present each heading the entity expects to use and the subtotals required by paras 69–74, despite IAS 34 para 10, until the first IFRS 18 annual financial statements are issued; interim reports also reconcile each statement of profit or loss line item for the comparative and cumulative comparative periods. Reconciliations for the current or earlier periods are permitted, not required. IFRS 18 · para C4–C5 IFRS 18 · para C6 Fully retrospective, with reconciliations for certain comparative periods: IFRS 18 and consequential amendments are effective for periods beginning on or after 1 January 2027 and apply fully retrospectively ; transitional provisions require the IAS 1 → IFRS 18 reconciliation for certain comparative periods and set interim requirements for the first year; earlier application permitted and disclosed. Detail → Ch8 . IFRS 18 · para C2–C5 EY Closer look 2026 · Overview Banks / insurers main-business-activity requirements. See also Ch3 3.5 overview IFRS 18 · para 49–51 IFRS 18 · para 55–58 IFRS 18 · para 65–66"
