    "href": "../ifrs-18/draft-v1-linked/ch02.html#s-2-1-3",
    "text": "2.1.3 — What the notes provide — understanding line items and supplementing the PFS Note role What the Standard lists Practical examples Understand presented line items (paragraph 17(a)) (a) Disaggregation of line items presented in the PFS; (b) descriptions of the characteristics of those line items; (c) information about the methods, assumptions and judgements used in recognising, measuring and presenting the items included in the PFS. IFRS 18 · para B6 Disaggregated inventory classifications such as work in progress and finished goods; valuation assumptions used to measure contingent consideration in a business combination. KPMG FI 2024 · section 4.1 EY Closer look 2026 · section 2.1.2 EY iGAAP 2026 Ch04 · section 2.1.2 Supplement — specifically required (paragraph 17(b)) Information specifically required by IFRS Accounting Standards — for example IAS 37 information about unrecognised contingent assets and contingent liabilities, and IFRS 7 information about exposure to credit risk, liquidity risk and market risk. IFRS 18 · para B7(a) IFRS 18 · para 19 Supplementary disclosures may not relate directly to a presented line item but are otherwise necessary — for example exposure to financial risks. KPMG FI 2024 · section 4.1 EY Closer look 2026 · section 2.1.2 EY iGAAP 2026 Ch04 · section 2.1.2 Supplement — additional information Information additional to the specific requirements, when compliance with them is insufficient for users to understand the effect of transactions and other events and conditions on financial position and financial performance. IFRS 18 · para B7(b) IFRS 18 · para 20 Continues the IAS 1 requirement to consider additional disclosures. EY Closer look 2026 · section 2.1.2 EY iGAAP 2026 Ch04 · section 2.1.2 The notes provide required content, may form a separate section, and include entity information if it is not published elsewhere with the financial statements. Required note content: the notes disclose (a) The basis of preparation (IAS 8 paragraphs 6A–6N) and the specific accounting policies used (IAS 8 paragraphs 27A–27I); (b) Information required by IFRS Accounting Standards that is not presented in the PFS; and (c) Other information not presented in the PFS but necessary to understand any of them IFRS 18 · para 113 Separate section permitted: notes about the basis of preparation and specific accounting policies may be disclosed in a separate section of the financial statements. IFRS 18 · para 115 Entity information, if not published elsewhere with the financial statements: domicile and legal form, country of incorporation and registered office address (or principal place of business, if different); nature of operations and principal activities; name of the parent and the ultimate parent of the group; and, for a limited-life entity, the length of its life. IFRS 18 · para 116"
