    "href": "../ifrs-18/draft-v1-linked/ch02.html#s-2-1-4",
    "text": "2.1.4 — Cross-references and systematic notes Cross-references signpost in both directions, which is expected to improve transparency, and the notes follow a systematic order as far as practicable. Signposting in both directions: as under IAS 1, each item in the PFS is cross-referenced to any related information in the notes. IFRS 18 adds the reverse link — if amounts disclosed in a note are included in one or more PFS line items, the note discloses the line item(s) in which they are included — because users said it is important to understand how note amounts relate to PFS line items. IFRS 18 · para 114 IFRS 18 · para BC324 EY Closer look 2026 · section 2.1.3 EY iGAAP 2026 Ch04 · section 2.1.3 Expected effect: the new note-to-line-item reference is expected to improve transparency and make it easier for users to link note amounts to the PFS. EY Closer look 2026 · section 2.1.3 EY iGAAP 2026 Ch04 · section 2.1.3 Systematic manner, as far as practicable: in deciding the order of the notes, the entity considers understandability and comparability. There must be a system or reason behind the ordering and grouping — for example by importance to the entity, in line-item order, or a combination. Ordering for understandability can reduce comparability; consistency of an entity’s note order from period to period is important, and a change in order should generally result from a specific event or transaction, such as a change in business. IFRS 18 · para 114 IFRS 18 · para BCZ322 Systematic ordering example Content (a) Prominence to key activities Give prominence to the areas of activity the entity considers most important to understanding its financial performance and financial position — for example, grouping information about particular business activities. IFRS 18 · para B112 (b) Similar measurement Group information about items measured similarly, such as assets measured at fair value. IFRS 18 · para B112 (c) Line-item order Follow the order of the line items in the statement(s) of financial performance and the statement of financial position: (i) statement of compliance (IAS 8 paragraph 6B); (ii) material accounting policy information (IAS 8 paragraph 27A); (iii) supporting information for PFS items, in statement order and line-item order; (iv) other disclosures — contingent liabilities (IAS 37) and unrecognised contractual commitments, and non-financial disclosures such as financial risk management objectives and policies (IFRS 7). IFRS 18 · para B112"
