    "chapter": "Chapter 2 — PFS roles & aggregation",
    "href": "../ifrs-18/draft-v1-linked/ch02.html#s-2-2",
    "text": "2.2 Additional line items and subtotals on the PFS Additional presentation is a structured-summary decision. Apply the required statement structure first, then ask whether the PFS would still be useful without an additional line item or subtotal. IFRS 18 · para 21–24 Additional line items and subtotals on the PFS follow four rules. Keep the required structure, do not separate mechanically, add when necessary, and accept that more or fewer line items depends on facts and circumstances. Keep the required structure. To provide a useful structured summary, each statement complies with the requirements that determine its structure: (a) Statement of profit or loss — paragraphs 47, 69, 76 and 78; (b) Statement presenting comprehensive income — paragraphs 86–88; (c) Statement of financial position — paragraphs 96 and 104; (d) Statement of changes in equity — paragraph 107; (e) Statement of cash flows — IAS 7 paragraph 10. Some requirements are always necessary for a useful structured summary — for example the classification of income and expenses into categories and the totals and subtotals required by paragraph 69 — so the entity does not assess them IFRS 18 · para 22 IFRS 18 · para BC56 EY Closer look 2026 · section 2.1.1 EY iGAAP 2026 Ch04 · section 2.1.1 Do not separate mechanically. A specified line item need not be presented separately if separate presentation is not necessary for a useful structured summary, even if the requirement calls it a minimum. IFRS 18 · para 23 Add when necessary. Present additional line items and subtotals when necessary for a useful structured summary. They must comprise amounts recognised and measured under IFRS Accounting Standards, fit the statement structure, be consistent period to period, and be no more prominent than required totals and subtotals. IFRS 18 · para 24 More or fewer line items — it depends on facts and circumstances. KPMG and EY both frame the new role as a judgement about whether a line contributes to an understandable overview, comparison, or a cue to seek note information; the answer can be more or fewer lines depending on facts and circumstances. KPMG FI 2024 · section 4.1 EY Closer look 2026 · section 2.1.1 EY iGAAP 2026 Ch04 · section 2.1.1 Decision If yes If no Does the separate line improve the overview? Present it if necessary for a useful structured summary. Do not separate mechanically; assess the notes for material detail. IFRS 18 · para 16 IFRS 18 · para 21–24 Does it support comparison? Separate presentation may make comparison between entities or periods more useful. Keep the structure proportionate and avoid clutter. IFRS 18 · para 16(b) IFRS 18 · para B8 Does it flag a note area? Present the line and use the notes to provide material explanation or disaggregation. Provide the material information in the notes if it is not on the PFS. IFRS 18 · para 16(c) IFRS 18 · para 17–18 IFRS 18 · para 42 Is an additional subtotal compatible? Present consistently, with IFRS-based amounts and no undue prominence. Do not add a subtotal merely because it is familiar or useful outside the financial statements. IFRS 18 · para 24 IFRS 18 · para B9"
