    "text": "2.2.1 — Required line items — material first, then the useful structured summary Paragraph 75 lists line items for the statement of profit or loss and paragraph 103 lists line items for the statement of financial position — now including goodwill (previously not in the IAS 1 paragraph 54 list). Paragraph 96 now refers to a useful structured summary instead of reliable and more relevant for a liquidity-order statement of financial position. Statement of financial position detail is in Ch7 7.2 . IFRS 18 · para 75 IFRS 18 · para 103 IFRS 18 · para 103(d) IFRS 18 · para 96 KPMG FI 2024 · section 4.1 EY Closer look 2026 · section 2.1.1 EY iGAAP 2026 Ch04 · section 2.1.1 Question Outcome Step 1. Which required line items are material? A required line item whose information is not material need not be presented or disclosed, even if described as a minimum requirement. IFRS 18 · para 19 EY Closer look 2026 · section 2.1.1.A EY iGAAP 2026 Ch04 · section 2.1.1.A Step 2. Is presenting each material required line item necessary for the statement to provide a useful structured summary? If yes, present it. If no, it need not be presented separately — but it is disclosed in the notes if the resulting information is material. IFRS 18 · para 23 IFRS 18 · para B8 IFRS 18 · para 42 EY Closer look 2026 · section 2.1.1.A EY iGAAP 2026 Ch04 · section 2.1.1.A Even “minimum” line items can be omitted from the face, as impairment losses illustrate, yet specific line items remain the starting point and the judgements involved can be difficult. Why even “minimum” line items can be omitted from the face: there may be situations where presenting those line items would not result in a statement that provides a useful structured summary. IFRS 18 · para BC57 Impairment losses example: if an entity concludes that presenting impairment losses determined under IFRS 9 is not necessary for a useful structured summary of income and expenses, it discloses those losses in the notes if that provides material information. IFRS 18 · para BC58 EY Closer look 2026 · section 2.1.1.A EY iGAAP 2026 Ch04 · section 2.1.1.A Specific line items remain the starting point: IFRS 18 and other Standards continue to require specific line items (for example revenue in the statement of profit or loss and property, plant and equipment in the statement of financial position); the PFS role guides whether material information is presented or disclosed. KPMG FI 2024 · section 4.1 Difficult judgements: the interaction between required line items, materiality and the useful structured summary involves nuances that are not always easy to reflect in practice; deciding whether to present, disclose or exclude information will in some cases involve difficult judgements. EY Closer look 2026 · section 2.1.1.A EY iGAAP 2026 Ch04 · section 2.1.1.A"
