    "text": "2.2.2 — Additional line items and subtotals — four constraints Constraint Requirement Application point (a) IFRS amounts Comprise amounts recognised and measured in accordance with IFRS Accounting Standards. IFRS 18 · para 24(a) IAS 1 had similar requirements for additional subtotals; IFRS 18 extends them to additional line items. Neither IFRS 18 nor its Basis for Conclusions explains what in accordance with IFRS Accounting Standards means. EY Closer look 2026 · section 2.1.1.B (b) Structure-compatible Be compatible with the statement structure created by the requirements listed in paragraph 22. IFRS 18 · para 24(b) Not previously in IAS 1. A subtotal such as ‘gross profit net of income taxes’ mixes the operating and income taxes categories and so conflicts with the requirement. Subtotal compatibility in the statement of profit or loss: Ch4 4.5 . EY Closer look 2026 · section 2.1.1.B EY iGAAP 2026 Ch04 · section 2.1.1.B (c) Consistent Be consistent from period to period, in accordance with paragraph 30. IFRS 18 · para 24(c) IFRS 18 · para 30 Additional line items and subtotals are retained from one period to the next unless a change in presentation is warranted. EY Closer look 2026 · section 2.1.1.B EY iGAAP 2026 Ch04 · section 2.1.1.B (d) Not more prominent Be displayed no more prominently than the totals and subtotals required by IFRS Accounting Standards. IFRS 18 · para 24(d) One of the four conditions the IASB added because some additional subtotals not specified in IFRS Accounting Standards can be misleading. IFRS 18 · para BC60 The four constraints on additional line items and subtotals exist because stakeholders said some unspecified subtotals can be misleading, and they supplement fair presentation. Several factors enter the judgement, and additional line items reach beyond paragraphs 75 and 103. Why the constraints exist: stakeholders told the IASB that some additional subtotals not specified in IFRS Accounting Standards can be misleading, so the IASB restricted additional line items and subtotals to those meeting the four conditions. IFRS 18 · para BC60 Supplements fair presentation: the requirements for additional line items and subtotals supplement the fair presentation requirements moved from IAS 1 to IAS 8. IFRS 18 · para BC61 EY Closer look 2026 · section 2.1.1.B EY iGAAP 2026 Ch04 · section 2.1.1.B Factors in the judgement: entity-specific circumstances, common practice among peers and the information needs of users; the assessment involves significant judgement, and regulators in many jurisdictions may scrutinise the basis for including additional line items and subtotals in the financial statements rather than only communicating them outside. EY Closer look 2026 · section 2.1.1.B Beyond paragraphs 75 and 103: additional line items are presented when necessary for a useful structured summary of income and expenses, or of assets, liabilities and equity, using the characteristics in 2.3.2 and the examples in 2.3.3 . IFRS 18 · para B9 IFRS 18 · para B78–B79 IFRS 18 · para B109–B111"
