    "text": "2.3.3 — Items that might need separate presentation or disclosure B79 and B111 give examples of items that might have sufficiently dissimilar characteristics that separate presentation in the PFS (for a useful structured summary) or separate disclosure in the notes (for material information) is necessary. The lists are examples, not exhaustive, and not every item applies to every entity. IFRS 18 · para 42 IFRS 18 · para B79 IFRS 18 · para B111 EY Closer look 2026 · section 2.2.2.B EY iGAAP 2026 Ch04 · section 2.2.2.B Income and expenses Assets, liabilities and equity (a) Write-downs of inventories, and reversals of such write-downs. IFRS 18 · para B79(a) (a) Property, plant and equipment disaggregated into classes under IAS 16. IFRS 18 · para B111(a) (b) Impairment losses for property, plant and equipment, and reversals. IFRS 18 · para B79(b) (b) Receivables disaggregated into amounts from trade customers, amounts from related parties, prepayments and other amounts. IFRS 18 · para B111(b) (c) Income and expenses from restructurings, and reversals of restructuring provisions. IFRS 18 · para B79(c) (c) Inventories disaggregated under IAS 2 into merchandise, production supplies, materials, work in progress and finished goods. IFRS 18 · para B111(c) (d) Income and expenses from disposals of property, plant and equipment. IFRS 18 · para B79(d) (d) Trade payables disaggregated, applying IAS 7, to show separately the amounts that are part of supplier finance arrangements — Illustration 2.3.4 . IFRS 18 · para B111(d) (e) Income and expenses from disposals of investments. IFRS 18 · para B79(e) (e) Provisions disaggregated by nature — employee benefits, decommissioning liabilities or other items. IFRS 18 · para B111(e) (f) Income and expenses from litigation settlements. IFRS 18 · para B79(f) (f) Equity capital and reserves disaggregated into classes such as paid-in capital, share premium and reserves. IFRS 18 · para B111(f) (g) Reversals of provisions. IFRS 18 · para B79(g) — (h) Non-recurring income and expenses not included in (a)–(g). IFRS 18 · para B79(h) — Non-recurring items are now explicit, but IFRS 18 gives no definition of ‘unusual’. Non-recurring items are now explicit: IAS 1 already required presentation or disclosure of material items of income or expense; B79(h) explicitly adds non-recurring income and expenses as potentially dissimilar, so entities may need to consider non-recurring items when deciding what to present or disclose separately. IFRS 18 · para B79(h) KPMG FI 2024 · section 4.1 No definition of ‘unusual’: the IASB sought to define unusual income and expenses but abandoned the attempt because stakeholder views differed; it expects disclosure about unusual items to improve through the disaggregation and labelling requirements — an entity describing items as ‘unusual’ explains what it means by the term ( 2.4 ). IFRS 18 · para BC78 KPMG FI 2024 · section 4.1 Illustration: 2.3.4 — Reverse factoring payables grouping KPMG FI 2024 · Example 5 / section 4.2 IFRS 18 · para 41–43 IFRS 18 · para B17 IFRS 18 · para B111(d) IAS 7 · para 44F / 44H Facts Entity X enters into a reverse factoring (supplier finance) arrangement with Finance Provider Y for some of its trade payables — Y pays X’s suppliers; X pays Y on the same date or later. Such arrangements typically give the entity extended payment terms compared with the invoice due date, or give the supplier the benefit of early payment. X must decide statement of financial position presentation and note disclosure for those payables. Characteristics considered against other trade payables: nature, function, measurement basis and size. Assessment Face aggregation acceptable. Characteristics are sufficiently similar to other trade payables, so a separate line item is not necessary for a useful structured summary of liabilities. Judgement on X’s facts. X presents one trade-payables line item comprising payables subject to the arrangement and those that are not. Notes still needed. Characteristics are also sufficiently dissimilar that note disclosure gives material information. Outcome Face: one aggregated trade-payables line item. Notes: disaggregated amounts subject to the arrangement, the terms and conditions, the due dates (IAS 7 paragraphs 44F and 44H) and other relevant information. Characteristics test, not habit: aggregation follows paragraphs 41–43 and B17, not “same caption as last year”; B111(d) names supplier finance payables as a candidate for separate disclosure."
