    "text": "2.3.6 — Foreign exchange differences — same line or separate line Foreign exchange differences follow the category of the item that gave rise to them (classification: Ch3 3.1 ; category detail: Ch3 3.7.5 ). Within a category, should they be (a) included in the same line item as the underlying transaction — for example in cost of sales for a trade payable for inventory — or (b) presented as a separate ‘foreign exchange differences’ line item in each category, on the basis that they are sufficiently dissimilar? IFRS 18 · para B65–B76 EY Closer look 2026 · section 2.2.2 · Q2-2 Whether foreign exchange differences go on the same line or a separate line is judgemental, and note disclosure is required either way. Judgemental: the aggregation and disaggregation requirements are balanced against the need for a useful structured summary, considering the materiality guidance and the requirements to present specific line items; each entity considers its own facts and circumstances, relevant industry practice and the views of local regulators. IFRS 18 · para B1–B5 EY Closer look 2026 · section 2.2.2 · Q2-2 Note disclosure either way: entities with material foreign exchange differences disclose in the notes the line item(s) in the statement of profit or loss in which they are included (EY also refers to IAS 21 paragraph 52). IFRS 18 · para 114 EY Closer look 2026 · section 2.2.2 · Q2-2"
