    "href": "../ifrs-18/draft-v1-linked/ch02.html#s-2-4-fig7",
    "text": "2.4.2 — Informative labels for aggregated items Figure 7 sets out how to determine informative labels and information for aggregated items , so that aggregation does not obscure a useful structured summary; it accompanies IFRS 18 and is not part of it. KPMG’s flowchart and EY Figure 2-1 follow the same path. IFRS 18 · Figure 7 IFRS 18 · para B25–B26 IFRS 18 · para B26(a) IFRS 18 · para 41 IFRS 18 · para B26(b) KPMG FI 2024 · section 4.3 EY Closer look 2026 · Fig 2-1 / section 2.3 EY iGAAP 2026 Ch04 · Fig 2-1 / section 2.3 Decision Yes path No path Is there a more informative label than ‘other’? Use the informative label for the aggregated item — do not default to ‘other’. Use a label that describes the aggregated item as precisely as possible (e.g. ‘other operating expenses’ or ‘other finance expenses’). Do the aggregated items comprise only items for which information is not material? Ask whether the aggregated amount is sufficiently large that users might reasonably question whether it includes items for which information could be material. Disclose material information. Amount sufficiently large that users might question materiality? Provide further information (e.g. explain that no material items are included; or that the amount comprises several immaterial items, with an indication of the nature and amount of the largest item). No further consideration needed. A large immaterial aggregate needs explanation, and ‘other’ serves only as a last-resort label. Why a large immaterial aggregate needs explanation: an entity might aggregate individually immaterial items with dissimilar characteristics into an amount that is cumulatively large; if users would reasonably question whether it includes material amounts, the information that resolves that question is itself material. IFRS 18 · para BC80 EY Closer look 2026 · section 2.3.1 EY iGAAP 2026 Ch04 · section 2.3.1 Last-resort label: ‘other’ is used only when no more informative label can be found — Figure 7 is a labelling and materiality path, not a licence to hide dissimilar material items. IFRS 18 · para B25"
