    "text": "3.1 Five categories — the P&L bands The Standard lists five categories, three of which are new. An entity shall classify income and expenses included in the statement of profit or loss in one of five categories : operating, investing, financing, income taxes and discontinued operations. IFRS 18 · para 47 The Standard lists five categories, the Big4 align on them, and KPMG gives each a one-line description. A key premise underpins the bands, and no category labels are forced on the face. Standard list. Categories (a)–(e) in paragraph 47 point to the detailed classification rules in paragraphs 52–68; Appendix B supplements the bands (B29) and the FX / net-monetary / derivatives path (B65–B76). IFRS 18 · para 47–48 IFRS 18 · para B29 Big4 alignment. KPMG and EY both frame the same five-category set: three new categories (operating, investing, financing) plus the existing income taxes and discontinued operations categories; required subtotals sit across that structure (detail in Ch4). KPMG FI 2024 · section 2.1 EY Closer look 2026 · section 3.1.1 KPMG’s one-line descriptions. Operating — income and expenses from the main business activities and anything not classified elsewhere; investing — income and expenses from investments made individually and largely independently of the main business activities; financing — income and expenses relating to obtaining finance to fund the main business activities and/or investing activities; income tax — tax expense or income and related FX differences; discontinued operation — income and expenses from discontinued operations. KPMG FI 2024 · section 2.1 Key premise. The operating category, and therefore operating profit, provides a complete picture of an entity’s operations; the specified-main-business-activity assessment exists so that it can. Entities with several main business activities, including a specified one, apply both the general and the specific requirements, so classification may be more complex. KPMG FI 2024 · section 2.1 IFRS 18 · para B30 No forced category labels on the face. The Board concluded there is no requirement to label the categories on the statement of profit or loss, nor to present a subtotal for each category; similar labels across statements (e.g. IAS 7) are intentionally not aligned. IFRS 18 · para BC86–BC87 EY Closer look 2026 · section 3.1 Category Standard meaning Teaching one-liner Operating All income and expenses in P&L that are not classified in the other four categories. IFRS 18 · para 52 Default / residual — complete operations picture, not “recurring only.” IFRS 18 · para 52 IFRS 18 · para IN9 IFRS 18 · para B42 KPMG FI 2024 · section 2.1.2.1 EY Closer look 2026 · section 3.2.3 EY iGAAP 2026 Ch04 · section 3.2.3 Investing Income and expenses from associates/JVs/unconsol. subsidiaries; cash & cash equivalents; and other assets that generate a return individually and largely independently — subject to specified-MBA overrides. IFRS 18 · para 53–58 Stand-alone investment returns separated from the operating story. IFRS 18 · para 53–54 IFRS 18 · para IN10 KPMG FI 2024 · section 2.1.2.2 EY Closer look 2026 · section 3.2.1 Financing Income/expenses from liabilities that involve only the raising of finance, plus specified interest-like amounts on other liabilities — subject to specified-MBA overrides and the paragraph 63–64 exclusions. IFRS 18 · para 59–66 Financing effects separated so users can analyse performance before financing. IFRS 18 · para 59–61 IFRS 18 · para IN11 KPMG FI 2024 · section 2.1.2.3 EY Closer look 2026 · section 3.2.2 EY iGAAP 2026 Ch04 · section 3.2.2 Income taxes Tax expense or tax income included in P&L applying IAS 12, and any related foreign exchange differences. IFRS 18 · para 67 Tax band — not mixed into operating. IFRS 18 · para 67 IFRS 18 · para B65–B68 KPMG FI 2024 · section 2.1 EY Closer look 2026 · section 3.2.4 EY iGAAP 2026 Ch04 · section 3.2.4 Discontinued operations Income and expenses from discontinued operations as required by IFRS 5. IFRS 18 · para 68 IFRS 5 bridge — amounts in this category are not re-tested into operating/investing/financing. IFRS 18 · para 68 IFRS 18 · para B29 KPMG FI 2024 · section 2.1 EY Closer look 2026 · section 3.2.5 EY iGAAP 2026 Ch04 · section 3.2.5 FX and derivative gains and losses bridge into the related item’s category, and classification applies only to P&L amounts. FX / derivatives bridge. Paragraph 48 points to B65–B76 for foreign exchange differences, the gain or loss on the net monetary position, and gains and losses on derivatives and designated hedging instruments. Classify these with the related item’s category (undue cost or effort may push FX into operating); the full rules are in 3.7 . IFRS 18 · para 48 IFRS 18 · para B65–B76 EY Closer look 2026 · section 3.1.1 EY iGAAP 2026 Ch04 · section 3.1.1 KPMG FI 2024 · section 2.1.6–2.1.7 Classification only for P&L amounts. The category requirements apply to income and expenses included in profit or loss (including recycling from OCI); they do not apply to amounts capitalised to an asset or remaining in OCI. EY Closer look 2026 · section 3.1 EY iGAAP 2026 Ch04 · section 3.1 Concept insight: The statement of profit or loss has five category bands; required subtotals (operating profit; profit or loss before financing and income taxes; profit or loss) are added across that structure — detail in Ch4. IFRS 18 · para 47 IFRS 18 · para 69"
