    "chapter": "Chapter 3 — P&L categories",
    "href": "../ifrs-18/draft-v1-linked/ch03.html#s-3-2-2",
    "text": "3.2.2 — Operating profit subtotal — required, but not directly defined Operating profit is a required subtotal and a consistent starting point rather than management’s view. IFRS 18 gives no direct definition because one would be near impossible for all entities, allows a one-way exception, may still change existing subtotals, and permits alternative labels. Required subtotal. Present operating profit or loss, comprising all income and expenses classified in the operating category. The subtotal was introduced to provide decision-useful information, reduce diversity and enhance comparability: today’s operating measures “can vary quite significantly across entities”. IFRS 18 · para 69(a) IFRS 18 · para 70 IFRS 18 · para BC88 EY Closer look 2026 · section 3.2.3.A EY iGAAP 2026 Ch04 · section 3.2.3.A A consistent starting point, not management’s view. The Board accepted differing views on what operating profit should contain; other tools carry those views — additional line items or subtotals, further disaggregation, and MPMs (e.g. operating profit excluding expenses regarded as non-recurring or unusual). IFRS 18 · para BC93 EY Closer look 2026 · section 3.2.3.A EY iGAAP 2026 Ch04 · section 3.2.3.A Why no direct definition. A direct definition would be “near impossible” to make appropriate for all entities; it would need significant judgement — for example, a by-function presenter might leave out an expense not allocated to a function line. Defining investing and financing reduces judgement over operating. IFRS 18 · para BC89 IFRS 18 · para BC91 EY Closer look 2026 · section 3.2.3.A EY iGAAP 2026 Ch04 · section 3.2.3.A One-way exception. Specified main business activities pull some amounts into operating; the reverse does not apply — an entity cannot exclude income and expenses from operating because they do not arise from its main business activities. IFRS 18 · para BC90 EY Closer look 2026 · section 3.2.3.A EY iGAAP 2026 Ch04 · section 3.2.3.A Existing subtotals may still change. EY view: entities that already present operating profit cannot presume its content will not change — for example, presenting the share of profit of equity-accounted associates and joint ventures in operating is not permissible under IFRS 18. EY Closer look 2026 · section 3.2.3.A EY iGAAP 2026 Ch04 · section 3.2.3.A Alternative labels. Required totals and subtotals may carry other labels that faithfully represent the items (IFRS 18 gives ‘net income’ for profit or loss). EY view: ‘operating result’ and ‘net operating income’ are acceptable for operating profit, provided they have no different connotation in the jurisdiction. IFRS 18 · para 11 IFRS 18 · para 43 EY Closer look 2026 · section 3.2.3.A · Q3-18 EY iGAAP 2026 Ch04 · section 3.2.3.A · Q3-14"
