    "href": "../ifrs-18/draft-v1-linked/ch03.html#s-3-3-6",
    "text": "3.3.6 — Common assets — leased PPE and finance-lease receivables Fact pattern Category Why Entity L , a manufacturer without an investing MBA, leases out a machine it no longer needs under an IFRS 16 operating lease. Investing B48 assumes PPE is used in the entity’s own operations; a lessor that leases out an individual item and does not use it can earn individual, largely independent returns. EY view. IFRS 18 · para 53(c) IFRS 18 · para 54(a) IFRS 18 · para B48 EY Closer look 2026 · section 3.2.1.E · Q3-6 Entity C , a construction company, leases out one excavator for the two-month summer shutdown. Operating The unit of account is the asset, not the return. Most of the excavator’s returns come from use in construction, so all its income and expenses are operating, even though the short lease income looks independent. IFRS 18 · para B45 EY Closer look 2026 · section 3.2.1.E · Q3-7 Entity R , a retailer without a specified MBA, leases a former warehouse under a finance lease; the warehouse is derecognised and the net investment is a new unit of account. Investing (finance income) A net investment typically is not used in combination and does not arise from operating revenue activities, so its finance income — subsequent measurement — is investing. Judgement on origin can change this. IFRS 18 · para 53(c) IFRS 18 · para 54(b) IFRS 18 · para B48 EY Closer look 2026 · section 3.2.1.E · Q3-8 Entity S sells and installs industrial equipment and offers finance leases as part of its revenue activities; financing is not a main business activity. May be operating EY view: the net investment could be seen as arising from supplying services classified in operating, so not largely independent. IFRS 18 · para B48(b) IFRS 18 · para BC143 IFRS 18 · para B49(b) EY Closer look 2026 · section 3.2.1.E · Q3-8 Entities with an investing or customer-financing main business activity classify these amounts differently — see 3.5.9 . The selling profit on entering a finance lease follows the derecognition rule in 3.7.1 . EY Closer look 2026 · section 3.3.2.C · Q3-25 EY iGAAP 2026 Ch04 · section 3.3.2.B · Q3-18"
