    "chapter": "Chapter 3 — P&L categories",
    "href": "../ifrs-18/draft-v1-linked/ch03.html#s-3-3-9",
    "text": "3.3.9 — Subtotals inside and after investing Investing needs no heading and allows additional subtotals, and profit or loss before financing and income taxes follows it as a required subtotal. No heading required; additional subtotals allowed. There is no requirement to head the investing category, and additional subtotals within it are permitted where they provide a useful structured summary. EY view: this lets entities show how relevant different investments are to their business. IFRS 18 · para BC120 EY Closer look 2026 · section 3.2.1.G EY iGAAP 2026 Ch04 · section 3.2.1 Profit or loss before financing and income taxes. Mandatory, comprising operating profit and all investing income and expenses, so performance can be analysed independently of how the entity is financed. Present it even when it equals operating profit — mainly for digital reporting. Customer-financing entities may be prohibited from presenting it ( 3.5.15 ). IFRS 18 · para 71 IFRS 18 · para BC148 IFRS 18 · para BC152 EY Closer look 2026 · section 3.2.1.H EY iGAAP 2026 Ch04 · section 3.2.1.D"
