    "chapter": "Chapter 3 — P&L categories",
    "href": "../ifrs-18/draft-v1-linked/ch03.html#s-3-5",
    "text": "3.5 Specified main business activities Two linked ideas carry this section: what “main business activity” means as nested terms, and where that nest changes the ordered classification tests. The subsections then cover how to assess a specified main business activity, the investing-in-assets and customer-financing requirements, cash, and the bank, insurer and bancassurer cases. IFRS 18 · para 49–51 IFRS 18 · para B30–B41 The nest (part–whole). Three nested terms: operations (the operating category = residual default) contain main business activities (any — e.g. manufacturing, retail, services), which in turn contain only two specified main business activities. Ordinary main business activities need no test : their results already land in operating (except equity-accounted results). IFRS 18 · para 52 IFRS 18 · para B30 IFRS 18 · para B42 Nest — operations ⊃ MBA ⊃ specified MBA Only two specified MBAs are assessed, and the Standard explains why only these two. The answer is a matter of fact rather than assertion, evidence cues guide it, the assessment is made at reporting-entity level, and entities disclose the fact and any changes. Only two specified MBAs are assessed. Assess whether the entity has a specified main business activity of (a) investing in particular types of assets (investing in assets) or (b) providing financing to customers. IFRS 18 · para 49 IFRS 18 · para B30–B32 Why only these two. BC90: classifying income or expenses related to these main business activities in investing or financing would prevent the entity from presenting key operating-performance measures in operating; so some amounts are classified in operating instead. The reverse does not apply — operating was not designed to exclude amounts based on whether they arise from main business activities. IFRS 18 · para BC90 IFRS 18 · para IN12 Matter of fact, not assertion. Whether investing in assets or providing financing to customers is a main business activity is a matter of fact and not merely an assertion ; use judgement based on evidence. IFRS 18 · para B33 KPMG FI 2024 · section 2.1.1 EY Closer look 2026 · section 3.1.2 EY iGAAP 2026 Ch04 · section 3.1.2 Evidence cues. It is likely a main business activity if the entity uses a gross-profit-like subtotal that includes amounts which would otherwise sit in investing or financing as an important indicator of operating performance (externally or internally). Segment information under IFRS 8 may also provide evidence. Detail in 3.5.2 . IFRS 18 · para B34–B36 KPMG FI 2024 · section 2.1.1 Reporting-entity level. Assess for the reporting entity as a whole; a consolidated group and a subsidiary can have different outcomes. IFRS 18 · para B37 KPMG FI 2024 · section 2.1.1.1 Disclose the fact (and changes). Disclose if the entity invests in assets or provides financing to customers as a main business activity; if the assessment outcome changes, disclose the fact, date, and (unless impracticable) the before/after amounts and classifications. Changes apply prospectively. IFRS 18 · para 50–51 IFRS 18 · para B41 Where the nest meets the ordered tests. A specified MBA does not create a sixth band. On the ordered tests used across 3.2–3.6, answer no at the Investing / Financing tests when a specified MBA has already pulled that amount into Operating; the note under the path below points back to the nest . Use the path as a checklist of the Standard’s order, not as an extra pipeline. Classification path — ordered tests (SMBA note below) Ordered test If yes If no Discontinued operations? Classify in the discontinued operations category (IFRS 5). Do not re-test into operating/investing/financing. IFRS 18 · para B29 Continue. IFRS 18 · para 68 IFRS 18 · para B29 Income taxes (IAS 12 + related FX)? Classify in the income taxes category. Do not re-test into operating/investing/financing. IFRS 18 · para B29 Continue. IFRS 18 · para 67 IFRS 18 · para B65–B68 Investing asset set (paragraph 53) and no SMBA pull? Classify paragraph 54 amounts in investing (subject to paragraphs 55–58). If SMBA already pulled the amount into operating, answer “no” here and leave it in operating. IFRS 18 · para 53–58 Financing liability path (paragraphs 59–61) and no SMBA pull / paragraph 64 exclusion? Classify the specified financing amounts in financing (subject to paragraphs 63–66). If SMBA or paragraph 64 already pulled the amount into operating, answer “no” here. IFRS 18 · para 59–66 Else? Operating residual — complete operations picture for the period. IFRS 18 · para 52 IFRS 18 · para B42 Bank, insurer and bancassurer requirements. See also 3.5.17 3.5.19 3.5.21 IFRS 18 · para 55–58 IFRS 18 · para 65–66"
