    "text": "3.5.8 — Investing MBA classification Decision schematic (Official Figure 3.1) for income and expenses specified in paragraph 54 from cash and cash equivalents, investments in associates, JVs and unconsolidated subsidiaries, and other assets that generate a return individually and largely independently: Cash and cash equivalents Investments in associates, JVs and unconsolidated subsidiaries Other assets that generate a return individually and largely independently Decision Path Is the investment accounted for using the equity method? Yes → classify in the investing category (para 53 and 55(a)). No → ask whether investing in the asset is a main business activity (B38, B40). Investing in the asset is a main business activity? Yes → classify in the operating category (para 55(b) and 58). No → classify in the investing category (para 53 and 55(a)). Cash and cash equivalents See Figure 3.3 (3.5.16). Figure footnote Investments in associates, JVs and unconsolidated subsidiaries include such assets in consolidated and separate financial statements. IFRS 18 · Figure 3.1 IFRS 18 · para 53–58"
