    "text": "3.5.18 — Banks — recurring questions Question Answer Interest accrual on FVTPL instruments — separate line? EY view: yes, as a separate line in the same category if needed for a useful structured summary, under an IAS 8 policy set by class of instrument (not all FVTPL items together). It cannot be added to ‘interest revenue calculated using the effective interest method’ (IFRS IC, March 2018, carried forward). The same applies to swap interest accruals. IFRS 18 · para 24 IFRS 18 · para 75(b)(i) EY Closer look 2026 · section C.2 · Q C.2-1 EY Closer look 2026 · section C.2 · Q C.2-2 EY Closer look 2026 · section C.8 · Q C.8-1 Subsidiary-level MBA in a banking group A subsidiary’s investment-property MBA does not carry to the group if the group lacks indicators and the activity is small; the group classifies that income in investing. IFRS 18 · para B37 IFRS 18 · para BC98 EY Closer look 2026 · section C.3 · Q C.3-2 Cash and cash equivalents Financial-asset MBA → all operating; otherwise related cash operating, unrelated cash by policy consistent with liabilities; KPMG: if all financing liabilities are operating, all cash must be operating too. EY view: a conglomerate’s policy reaches cash of unrelated subsidiaries. IFRS 18 · para 56 IFRS 18 · para 57 EY Closer look 2026 · section C.4 · Q C.4-1 EY Closer look 2026 · section C.4 · Q C.4-2 KPMG FI 2024 · section 8.1.1.2 Which Type 1 liabilities fall under the choice EY Illustration C.5-1 repeats the Bank B pattern in 3.5.12 for “Bank A” (EY’s conclusion prints “Bank B”); the conglomerate question in Q C.5-1 cites “IFRS 16.56(a)” as printed. Policy is at reporting-entity level; not liability-by-liability. EY Closer look 2026 · Ill C.5-1 / section C.5 EY Closer look 2026 · section C.5 · Q C.5-1 Interest on borrowings; amortised cost vs FVTPL Classify IAS 32 financial liabilities first; bank borrowings are generally Type 1. Measurement category matters only for Type 2 liabilities (e.g. FVTPL contingent consideration → operating; amortised-cost payable with significant financing → financing interest). IFRS 18 · para 61 IFRS 18 · para BC168 EY Closer look 2026 · section C.5 · Q C.5-4 EY Closer look 2026 · section C.5 · Q C.5-5 Equity-accounted investments seen as operations Options: the IFRS 18 transition election to FVTPL for IAS 28.18-eligible entities; an additional subtotal within investing (an MPM unless it covers all equity-accounted investees); or a non-IFRS measure outside the statements. IFRS 18 · para C7 IFRS 18 · para BC367 IFRS 18 · para 118 EY Closer look 2026 · section C.6 · Q C.6-1 Undue cost or effort for FX Not defined; not a low hurdle (higher for publicly accountable entities); the more important the information, the higher the bar; assessed per item or transaction and at each reporting date. IFRS 18 · para B68 EY Closer look 2026 · section C.7 · Q C.7-1 Hybrids and derivatives Unseparated Type 1 hybrids follow the liability policy unless customer-related; banks’ hedges of customer loans and related liabilities → operating; hedges of unrelated liabilities follow those liabilities’ category. IFRS 18 · para B56–B57 IFRS 18 · para B70–B76 KPMG FI 2024 · section 8.1.1.4 KPMG FI 2024 · section 8.1.1.5 Origination and commitment fees received Operating — in interest income when part of the effective interest rate, otherwise in IFRS 15 fee income. IFRS 18 · para B48(c) IFRS 18 · para B49 EY Closer look 2026 · section C.9 · Q C.9-1 Expected credit losses outside operating? Depends on the asset: loans to customers → operating; investments held as an MBA → operating; without a specified MBA, receivables → operating and stand-alone investments → investing. IFRS 18 · para B77 IFRS 18 · para 58 EY Closer look 2026 · section C.9 · Q C.9-2 Link to the statement of cash flows For specified-MBA entities, dividends and interest cash flows follow the P&L category; where amounts sit in more than one category, a single-category policy choice applies to each of dividends received, interest received and interest paid. Dividends paid are always financing. IAS 7 · para 33A IAS 7 · para 34B IAS 7 · para 34D EY Closer look 2026 · section C.9 · Q C.9-3 Which bank measures are MPMs Net interest income and net fee and commission income are not MPMs; ratios are not, but an adjusted numerator (e.g. of return on equity) can be; ‘underlying profit’ or ‘profit before impairment’ can be. Detail in Ch6. IFRS 18 · para 118 IFRS 18 · para B117 KPMG FI 2024 · section 8.1.2 EY Closer look 2026 · section C.10 · Q C.10-1"
