    "text": "3.5.21 — Bancassurers Bancassurers generally have two MBAs, build their statement structure around them, and may adopt an all-operating policy. Two MBAs. A bancassurer generally invests in assets and provides financing to customers; insurance (often with asset management) and banking may be separate reportable segments, supporting both MBAs. IFRS 8 · para 13 IFRS 18 · para B33 IFRS 18 · para B36 KPMG FI 2024 · section 8.2.5 Structure. Additional subtotals such as net interest income, net fee and commission income and insurance service result sit inside operating; equity-accounted results are investing; interest not related to customer financing is financing if the policy keeps it there. KPMG FI 2024 · section 8.2.5 KPMG FI 2024 · section 8.2.1.6 All-operating policy. An entity that classifies all cash and financing-liability amounts in operating does not present profit before financing and income taxes; it might add ‘operating profit and income and expenses from investments accounted for under the equity method’ under paragraph 73. IFRS 18 · para 73 KPMG FI 2024 · section 8.2.5"
