    "chapter": "Chapter 3 — P&L categories",
    "href": "../ifrs-18/draft-v1-linked/ch03.html#s-3-7",
    "text": "3.7 Other requirements — derecognition, FX, net monetary position and derivatives Some income and expenses take their category from a related item rather than from their own nature. Paragraph 48 points to B65–B76 for foreign exchange differences, the gain or loss on the net monetary position, and gains and losses on derivatives and designated hedging instruments; B60–B64 cover derecognition, held-for-sale classification and change in use. KPMG groups these as the “other requirements” that sit on top of the category tests. IFRS 18 · para 48 IFRS 18 · para B65–B76 IFRS 18 · para B60–B64 KPMG FI 2024 · section 2.1.5 KPMG FI 2024 · section 2.1.6–2.1.7 EY Closer look 2026 · section 3.2.6 EY iGAAP 2026 Ch04 · section 3.2.6 On derecognition the ‘old’ category wins, operating catches what cannot be traced, and IAS 7 categories are not relabelled. Customer financiers have their own position. The ‘old’ category wins. Income and expenses from derecognition or a change in classification follow the category used for the asset or liability immediately before the event; foreign exchange differences and hedge results follow the item that gave rise to them or the risk managed. IFRS 18 · para BC202–BC203 IFRS 18 · para B65 IFRS 18 · para B70 Operating catches what cannot be traced. Undue cost or effort (FX, non-designated derivatives), grossing up (hedges and derivatives) and an unpresented net monetary position all fall back to operating, consistent with operating as the residual category. IFRS 18 · para B68 IFRS 18 · para B69 IFRS 18 · para B72 IFRS 18 · para BC213–BC215 Do not relabel IAS 7 categories. Investing/financing in P&L are not the IAS 7 cash-flow categories; similar words, different objectives. IFRS 18 · para BC86–BC87 Customer financiers. Entities that provide financing to customers as a main business activity have their own derecognition, FX and derivative points — see 3.5.15 . EY Closer look 2026 · section 3.3.3.I EY iGAAP 2026 Ch04 · section 3.3.3.C EY Closer look 2026 · section 3.3.3.J EY iGAAP 2026 Ch04 · section 3.3.3.D EY Closer look 2026 · section 3.3.3.K EY iGAAP 2026 Ch04 · section 3.3.3.E"
