    "href": "../ifrs-18/draft-v1-linked/ch03.html#s-3-7-1",
    "text": "3.7.1 — Derecognition and held for sale: single assets and liabilities Income and expenses from Category Why Disposal of property, plant and equipment used in operations Operating Depreciation was operating before disposal. IFRS 18 · para B60(a) Disposal of an investment property not invested in as a main business activity Investing Rental income was investing before disposal. IFRS 18 · para B60(b) Remeasurement to fair value of an equity-accounted associate on the step acquisition of a subsidiary Investing The associate’s income and expenses were investing before the step acquisition. IFRS 18 · para B60(c) IFRS 3 · para 42 Derecognition (e.g. prepayment) of a liability from a transaction that involves only the raising of finance, by an entity without a customer-financing main business activity Financing Same requirements as on recognition (paragraphs 52 and 59–60). IFRS 18 · para B61(a) Derecognition of a supplier payable on entering a supplier finance arrangement (and recognition of the new liability) Operating A gain or loss on derecognising a Type 2 liability is not interest identified for other Standards. IFRS 18 · para B61(b) IFRS 18 · para 61 IFRS 18 · para BC164 Selling profit or loss on entering a finance lease over property, plant and equipment Operating The asset did not previously generate individual, largely independent returns — irrespective of where finance income is classified after commencement. IFRS 18 · para B60 EY Closer look 2026 · section 3.2.6.A · Q3-19 EY iGAAP 2026 Ch04 · section 3.2.6.A · Q3-15 Selling profit or loss on entering a finance lease over an investment property previously leased out under an operating lease Investing Rental income from the property was investing before derecognition. EY Closer look 2026 · section 3.2.6.A · Q3-19 EY iGAAP 2026 Ch04 · section 3.2.6.A · Q3-15 The ‘old’ category applies to a single asset held for sale and to an associate held for sale, liabilities need their type classified first, and specified MBAs bring their own considerations. Held for sale (single asset). The ‘old’ category also applies to an individual asset classified as held for sale under IFRS 5: the impairment loss on classification, any later remeasurement while held for sale, and the gain or loss on ultimate disposal. IFRS 18 · para B47(g) IFRS 18 · para B49(e) IFRS 18 · para B60 EY Closer look 2026 · section 3.2.6 EY iGAAP 2026 Ch04 · section 3.2.6 KPMG FI 2024 · section 2.1.5.1 EY Closer look 2026 · section 3.2.6.B Associate held for sale. Equity accounting stops on held-for-sale classification. KPMG says the outcome is not entirely clear but that, arguably, income and expenses while held for sale (e.g. dividends, impairment losses) and on derecognition continue to be classified in investing. IFRS 18 · para B60 KPMG FI 2024 · section 2.1.5.1 Liabilities: classify the type first. On derecognition, apply the same requirements as on recognition — decide whether the liability is Type 1 or Type 2 ( 3.4 ), then follow that path. IFRS 18 · para B61 EY Closer look 2026 · section 3.2.6.B EY iGAAP 2026 Ch04 · section 3.2.6.B Specified main business activities. A finance-lease selling profit can land elsewhere for an entity with a specified main business activity — see 3.5.9 . EY Closer look 2026 · section 3.3.2.C · Q3-27 EY iGAAP 2026 Ch04 · section 3.3.2.B · Q3-20 Illustration: 3.7.2 — Gain or loss on disposal of selected assets EY Closer look 2026 · Ill 3-5 / section 3.2.6 EY iGAAP 2026 Ch04 · Ill 3-4 / section 3.2.6 IFRS 18 · para B60 IFRS 18 · para BC200 IFRS 18 · para BC202 Facts PPE: an entity sells an item of property, plant and equipment it used in its own operations. Investment property: an entity sells one of its investment properties. Step acquisition: an entity with an equity-accounted associate buys more shares and obtains control; IFRS 3 requires the associate to be remeasured to fair value immediately before the step acquisition. Assessment Each gain or loss follows the category of the expenses from that asset immediately before derecognition or the change. PPE depreciation was operating; investment property income was investing; the associate’s income and expenses were investing. Decision PPE disposal → operating. Investment property disposal → investing. Remeasurement gain or loss on the associate → investing."
