    "href": "../ifrs-18/draft-v1-linked/ch04.html#s-4-0",
    "text": "4.0 Scope — required totals vs para 118-listed vs MPM Once the five P&L categories exist (Ch3), lock the required totals and subtotals on the statement of profit or loss — and keep them separate from paragraph 118-listed (non-MPM) subtotals and from MPMs (Ch6). IFRS 18 requires presentation of operating profit or loss, profit or loss before financing and income taxes (subject to paragraph 73), and profit or loss. Separately, paragraph 118 lists commonly used income-and-expense subtotals that are not management-defined performance measures. MPMs follow a different disclosure regime. IFRS 18 · para 69–74 IFRS 18 · para 117–118 IFRS 18 · para IN8 IFRS 18 · para IN14 First decision — which required anchors? Present the three paragraph 69 measures on the face (with the paragraph 73 exception for the middle subtotal). IFRS 18 · para 69–72 Second decision — paragraph 118-listed or MPM? A useful subtotal of income and expenses may be IFRS-recognised under paragraph 118 (not an MPM) or may meet the paragraph 117 MPM definition and trigger the single-note reconciliation regime (Ch6). IFRS 18 · para 117–118 Third decision — additional face subtotals? Additional PFS subtotals are allowed only when necessary for a useful structured summary and must stay compatible with the category structure and required anchors. IFRS 18 · para 24 IFRS 18 · para B9 Fourth decision — which line items? Paragraph 75 lists the line items to present, filtered by the useful-structured-summary test; the same listed line item can appear in more than one category ( 4.3 ). IFRS 18 · para 75 IFRS 18 · para B77 Four building blocks. KPMG frames the topic as two new required profit subtotals, enhanced guidance on additional subtotals, the commonly presented subtotals listed in paragraph 118, and MPMs that are subtotals of income and expenses. KPMG FI 2024 · section 2.3 Pitfall: Equating “gross profit” (or similar) with an MPM. Gross profit or loss and the other paragraph 118 items are listed as not management-defined performance measures. IFRS 18 · para 118(a) IFRS 18 · para B123"
