    "chapter": "Chapter 5 — Operating expenses",
    "href": "../ifrs-18/draft-v1-linked/ch05.html#s-5-3-3",
    "text": "5.3.3 — Why five natures — alternatives the Board considered Alternative considered Board’s response Function information for nature presenters Not developed: little user demand, so costs would exceed benefits. IFRS 18 · para BC249 Each function line disaggregated by nature Useful for forecasting each line, but preparers said they generally do not track all expenses by nature; subsidiary-level nature data is lost on consolidation by function and through intercompany flows, so fundamental system changes would be needed. IFRS 18 · para BC262 Total operating expenses analysed by nature Expected to be cheaper than full disaggregation, but many preparers raised the same cost concerns. IFRS 18 · para BC263 Specified natures split by operating line (adopted) A better cost–benefit balance: preparers can provide a limited number of natures at reasonable cost, and users gain margin analysis, PFS-to-notes links and non-cash links to cash flows. IFRS 18 · para BC264–BC265 More natures than five Rejected: benefits often depend on industry and would not justify the extra cost. IFRS 18 · para BC267 A specific disclosure objective for the five Not set: it might require additional disclosures that jeopardise the cost–benefit balance. IFRS 18 · para BC276"
