    "chapter": "Chapter 6 — Management-defined performance measures (MPMs)",
    "href": "../ifrs-18/draft-v1-linked/ch06.html#s-6-1-fig6",
    "text": "6.1.1 — Identifying MPMs Decision schematic faithful to Official Figure 6, which accompanies but is not part of IFRS 18. Figure footnote: it is presumed that a subtotal of income and expenses used in public communications communicates management’s view (paragraph 119); an entity is not required to consider whether to rebut the presumption. Test If No / Yes → Is the measure a subtotal of income and expenses? (paragraph 117) No → not an MPM (disclosure requirements for MPMs not applicable). Yes → next. Used in public communications outside financial statements? (paragraph 117(a)) No → not an MPM. Yes → next. Listed in paragraph 118 or specifically required to be presented or disclosed by IFRS Accounting Standards? (paragraph 117(c)) Yes → not an MPM. No → next. Communicates management’s view of an aspect of the financial performance of the entity as a whole? (paragraph 117(b)) Presumed Yes if used in public communications (paragraph 119). If seeking to rebut: is there reasonable and supportable information to rebut (paragraph 120)? Yes (rebutted) → not an MPM. No → MPM — apply disclosure requirements. IFRS 18 · Figure 6 IFRS 18 · para 117–120"
