    "chapter": "Chapter 6 — Management-defined performance measures (MPMs)",
    "href": "../ifrs-18/draft-v1-linked/ch06.html#s-6-4-3",
    "text": "6.4.3 — Reconciliation layout, effort and regulators Topic Detail KPMG layout Columns for amount, tax effect and effect on NCI: adjusted operating profit (MPM) → restructuring costs (included in employee benefit expenses), with footnotes describing the programme and the statutory-rate tax basis → operating profit (required subtotal). IFRS 18 · para 123(c)–(e) KPMG FI 2024 · section 3.3 Format Not prescribed: the Board considered a columnar table adjusting each line item but left format to depend on the MPM. IFRS 18 · para BC382 KPMG FI 2024 · section 3.3 Effort KPMG view: the per-item tax and NCI effects may add effort; entities may want to revisit the subtotals they use publicly before adoption. IFRS 18 · para B141 IFRS 18 · para BC385–BC387 KPMG FI 2024 · section 3.3 Regulators KPMG: regulatory guidance may be more restrictive — e.g. the SEC non-GAAP rule prohibits certain measures (such as EBITDA and “special” EPS) in the FS; ESMA and IOSCO guidance is broadly aligned (clear description, reconciliation) but covers all financial non-GAAP measures, not only income-and-expense subtotals. KPMG FI 2024 · section 3.4"
