    "chapter": "Chapter 6 — Management-defined performance measures (MPMs)",
    "href": "../ifrs-18/draft-v1-linked/ch06.html#s-6-4-ex",
    "text": "6.4.4 — Is it an MPM, and what must the note show? Question Outcome Start. Identify a candidate subtotal of income and expenses used outside the FS (management commentary, press release, or investor presentation — not oral or social media). Candidate for the tests below. IFRS 18 · para 117 IFRS 18 · para B119 Test. (1) Subtotal of income and expenses? (2) Public communications outside FS? (3) Management’s view of entity-as-a-whole (paragraph 119 presumption; paragraph 120 rebuttal only with reasonable and supportable information)? (4) Not paragraph 118-listed and not IFRS-required? Run in order; any “no” stops the path. IFRS 18 · para 117–120 IFRS 18 · para 118 Output. Record the conclusion for each candidate. All tests pass → MPM: single note · describe aspect / usefulness · calculate · reconcile to closest paragraph 118 or IFRS measure · tax and NCI per reconciling item · tax methodology. Any test fails → not an MPM (may still be another metric or a paragraph 118 / required measure). IFRS 18 · para 122–123 IFRS 18 · para IN15"
