    "text": "6.6 Identify, disclose, change — the MPM sequence The MPM sequence runs identify, disclose and change, with face presentation as an optional path and interim reporting to follow. Identify. Income/expense subtotal? → public communications (B119 include/exclude)? → management view of entity-as-a-whole (paragraph 119 presumption / paragraph 120 rebuttal)? → not paragraph 118 / not IFRS-required? → MPM . IFRS 18 · para 117–120 IFRS 18 · para B116 IFRS 18 · para B119 Disclose. If MPM → single note · management statement · describe aspect / usefulness · calculate · reconcile · tax & NCI · tax methodology. IFRS 18 · para 122–123 Change. If calculation / addition / cessation / tax methodology changes → explain · reasons · restate (or impracticable disclosure). IFRS 18 · para 124–125 Face (optional path). MPM status ≠ automatic face presentation — paragraph 24 additional-subtotal criteria still bind; failing them means notes-only disclosure, still as an MPM. IFRS 18 · para B118 IFRS 18 · para 24 Interim. MPMs used in interim public communications need disclosure in the interim FS ( Ch7 7.4 ). IFRS 18 · para BC337"
