    "text": "7.1.4 — Indirect-method start and classification of interest and dividends Question Outcome Start. Preparing the statement of cash flows with the indirect method . Apply amended IAS 7 together with IFRS 18’s operating profit subtotal. IFRS 18 · para 70 IFRS 18 · App D Test. Does the reconciliation start from operating profit or loss as presented under paragraphs 69–70, then bridge to operating cash flows? Does the entity have a specified main business activity? Start from operating profit. Without a specified main business activity, use the fixed activities in 7.1.1 ; with one, follow the P&L ( 7.1.2 ). IFRS 18 · para 69–70 EY Closer look 2026 · section 5.1 EY iGAAP 2026 Ch04 · section 5.1 Output. Record the starting subtotal and the activity for each interest and dividend flow. Same operating starting point in the P&L and the statement of cash flows , not profit before tax; dividends paid in financing. KPMG FI 2024 · section 5.1"
