    "chapter": "Chapter 7 — Other FS impacts",
    "href": "../ifrs-18/draft-v1-linked/ch07.html#s-7-2-1",
    "text": "7.2.1 — SFP requirements carried forward and changed Requirement Paragraph Status under IFRS 18 Current / non-current, or order of liquidity when that is a more useful structured summary 96, B90–B93 Carried forward Disclose the amount recovered or settled after more than 12 months for each line item combining amounts within and after 12 months 97 Carried forward Deferred tax assets (liabilities) not classified as current 98 Carried forward Current asset and current liability criteria (operating cycle, trading, 12 months, cash; right to defer settlement) 99–102, B94–B108 Carried forward Minimum line items (a)–(s) 103 Carried forward, plus goodwill (d) as a new separate line item Non-controlling interests; issued capital and reserves attributable to owners of the parent 104 Carried forward Judgement on additional line items or note disclosure 105, B109–B111 Now framed by nature and function and the useful structured summary No prescribed order or format; descriptions may be amended 106 Carried forward Illustration: 7.2.2 — XYZ Group SFP (current / non-current) IFRS 18 · para 96 IFRS 18 · para IE7 SFP Facts XYZ Group’s statement of financial position at 31 December 20X2 (IE7), in thousands of CU, with 20X1 comparatives, using the current / non-current distinction (paragraph 96). IFRS 18 · para 96–106 IFRS 18 · para BCZ285 IFRS 18 · para BC313–BC315 IFRS 18 · Figure 1 KPMG FI 2024 · section 5.2 Goodwill (160,000) is presented separately from other intangible assets (158,400). Borrowings and lease liabilities are split between non-current and current; deferred tax liabilities (4,800) sit only in non-current. Assessment Current / non-current is one paragraph 96 path; order of liquidity is the other, when it gives a more useful structured summary. Separate goodwill meets paragraph 103(d); deferred tax only in non-current meets paragraph 98. Line items and aggregations must still meet the useful structured summary and characteristics tests ( Ch2 2.3 ). P&L categories apply only to profit or loss; SFP lines are classified current/non-current (or by liquidity), not operating, investing or financing. Decision Total assets 768,100 (20X1: 739,875) = non-current 650,600 + current 117,500; equity 293,600 + non-current liabilities 398,900 + current liabilities 75,600 agree. For an SFP aggregation example (reverse factoring), see Illustration 2.3.4 . Assets (in thousands of CU) 31 Dec 20X2 31 Dec 20X1 Non-current assets Property, plant and equipment 312,000 295,600 Goodwill 160,000 164,500 Other intangible assets 158,400 146,500 Investments in associates and joint ventures 20,200 17,400 Total non-current assets 650,600 624,000 Current assets Inventories 55,500 52,500 Trade receivables 34,000 32,000 Cash and cash equivalents 23,400 22,800 Other current assets 4,600 8,575 Total current assets 117,500 115,875 TOTAL ASSETS 768,100 739,875 Equity and liabilities (in thousands of CU) 31 Dec 20X2 31 Dec 20X1 Equity attributable to owners of the parent Share capital 110,000 100,000 Retained earnings 139,720 123,040 Other components of equity 2,480 4,740 Total equity attributable to owners of the parent 252,200 227,780 Non-controlling interests 41,400 34,995 Total equity 293,600 262,775 Non-current liabilities Borrowings 158,700 147,200 Lease liabilities 85,400 97,500 Pension liabilities 112,000 108,000 Provisions 38,000 32,000 Deferred tax liabilities 4,800 8,600 Total non-current liabilities 398,900 393,300 Current liabilities Borrowings 25,000 28,000 Lease liabilities 14,000 18,000 Payables for goods or services received and other payables 21,800 22,400 Provisions 9,700 10,600 Income taxes payable 5,100 4,800 Total current liabilities 75,600 83,800 Total liabilities 474,500 477,100 TOTAL EQUITY AND LIABILITIES 768,100 739,875"
