    "text": "7.3.3 — Can an additional amount per share be disclosed? Question Outcome Start. Identify the numerator of the proposed per-share amount (attributable to ordinary equity holders of the parent). Candidate for the tests below. IAS 33 · para 73B Test. Is the numerator a paragraph 69, 86 or 118 total or subtotal? If not, is it an MPM (including as a ratio numerator under B117)? Either “yes” → permitted; both “no” → not permitted. IFRS 18 · para 69 IFRS 18 · para 118 IFRS 18 · para B117 Output. If permitted, set the presentation. Notes only; basic and diluted with equal prominence; IAS 33 denominator; MPM disclosures if the numerator is an MPM. EY Closer look 2026 · section 5.3 EY iGAAP 2026 Ch04 · section 5.3 IFRS 18 · para 121–125"
