    "href": "../ifrs-18/draft-v1-linked/ch07.html#s-7-4-2",
    "text": "7.4.2 — Cross-referencing interim MPM disclosures to another report Point KPMG analysis Permitted? Yes. As for other IAS 34 paragraph 16A disclosures, MPM disclosures can be incorporated by cross-reference to another report (for example, management commentary) available to users on the same terms and at the same time as the interim statements. Content gap Management commentary may lack the required detail, for example the reconciliation to the most directly comparable paragraph 118 or required subtotal with tax and NCI effects for each reconciling item. Single note MPM information must be in a single note ( Ch6 6.4 ). Boundary Commentary may also include measures that are not MPMs (for example, free cash flows), making it hard to identify which measures form part of the interim statements and are subject to any assurance. KPMG FI 2024 · section 6.1 IFRS 18 · para 121–125"
