    "text": "8.3 Annual reconciliations (first IFRS 18 annual) In the first annual FS under IFRS 18, disclose for the comparative period immediately preceding first application a reconciliation for each P&L line item between: IFRS 18 · para C3 Restated amounts applying IFRS 18; and Amounts previously presented applying IAS 1. First IFRS 18 annual reconciliations are required so users can bridge to pre-IFRS 18 amounts and analyse trends, may include optional extras, can be shaped by local regulation, and affect systems. Why. The new P&L structure would make it hard for users to analyse trends without a bridge to the amounts presented before IFRS 18. IFRS 18 · para BC418 Optional extras. Reconciliations for the current period or earlier comparatives are permitted but not required. Requiring one for the year of first application would mean running IAS 1 systems for that whole year, at extra cost and with little benefit given retrospective application. IFRS 18 · para C6 IFRS 18 · para BC419–BC420 Local regulation. Where local rules require two comparative years, they may also require a reconciliation for every period presented. EY Closer look 2026 · section 6 EY iGAAP 2026 Ch04 · section 6 Systems. Comparative-period data must be capturable in IFRS 18 categories and subtotals, while the IAS 1 amounts previously presented form the other side of the reconciliation. KPMG FI 2024 · section 7.2 EY Closer look 2026 · section 6 EY iGAAP 2026 Ch04 · section 6"
