    "text": "8.4 Interim — first year of application In the first year, condensed interim statements present each heading the entity expects to use under IFRS 18 and the paragraphs 69–74 subtotals, despite IAS 34 paragraph 10, and disclose reconciliations for the comparative and cumulative comparative periods. IAS 34 paragraph 10 (same headings and subtotals as the most recent annual statements) is set aside for headings and subtotals until the first annual IFRS 18 financial statements are issued. IFRS 18 · para C4–C5 EY Closer look 2026 · section 6.1 EY iGAAP 2026 Ch04 · section 6.1 Interim headings change mid-year because the latest IAS 1 annual may carry different subtotals from those IFRS 18 requires, both periods are reconciled, the reconciliation has a set location, and the ongoing interim requirements are taught in Ch7. Why headings change mid-year. The most recent annual statements, still under IAS 1, may have different subtotals from those IFRS 18 requires; presenting the IFRS 18 subtotals gives users useful information. IFRS 18 · para BC421 Why both periods. Without reconciliations for both the comparative and the cumulative comparative period, users would struggle to understand interim comparatives and analyse trends; the Board judged the benefit worth the cost. IFRS 18 · para BC422 Where the reconciliation sits. It forms part of the IAS 34 paragraph 16A(a) disclosure (nature and effect of changes in accounting policies since the last annual period). EY Closer look 2026 · section 6.1 EY iGAAP 2026 Ch04 · section 6.1 IFRS 18 · para C5 Ongoing interim requirements. Aggregation and MPM disclosures in interim statements after the first year are in Ch7 7.4 . IFRS 18 · para 5"
