    "text": "8.5 IAS 28 fair value election on initial application At the date of initial application, an entity eligible under IAS 28 paragraph 18 may change its election for an associate or joint venture from the equity method to fair value through profit or loss under IFRS 9, retrospectively under IAS 8, and must make the same change in its separate financial statements (IAS 27 paragraph 11). IFRS 18 · para C7 EY Closer look 2026 · section 6 EY iGAAP 2026 Ch04 · section 6 The IAS 28 fair value election on initial application is open to eligible entities, exists as relief because some eligible entities chose the equity method before knowing how IFRS 18 would classify the income, affects operating profit, and comes with an eligibility clarification. Who is eligible. IAS 28 paragraph 18 covers investments held by, or indirectly through, venture capital organisations, mutual funds, unit trusts and similar entities, including investment-linked insurance funds. KPMG gives venture capital organisations, mutual funds and some insurers as examples. EY Closer look 2026 · section 3.3.5.A EY iGAAP 2026 Ch04 · section 3.3.5.A KPMG FI 2024 · section 7.2 Why the relief. The IAS 28 election is made per investment at initial recognition. Some eligible entities may have chosen the equity method before they knew how IFRS 18 would classify the income, so IFRS 18 lets them elect again on initial application. IFRS 18 · para BC423 EY Closer look 2026 · section 3.3.5.A EY iGAAP 2026 Ch04 · section 3.3.5.A Effect on operating profit. For an entity that invests in assets as a main business activity, income and expenses from associates and joint ventures at fair value are operating; under the equity method they are always investing. Electing fair value brings them into operating profit ( Ch3 3.3.2 ). KPMG FI 2024 · section 7.2 IFRS 18 · para BC423 Eligibility clarification. In February 2026 the IASB published ED/2026/1, Amendments to the Fair Value Option for Investments in Associates and Joint Ventures , proposing to clarify which entities are eligible. EY Closer look 2026 · section 3.3.5.A"
